{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "NO hook in .claude/settings.json INSTRUCTS a session to read, write, register in, or file into an archived path or retired skill. ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-09-21 AND THE CORRECTION MATTERS: the original criterion said the mention-counting grep must print NOTHING, and a CORRECT fix cannot satisfy that — the repaired hooks deliberately NAME the archived files in sentences saying they are archived and must not be used, because a session needs the name it would otherwise go hunting for. Measured after the fix: 22 mentions -> 8, and all 8 are warnings. A criterion that would have forced me to strip those warnings to go green was a criterion pushing toward a WORSE artifact, which is the thing a pre-registered rule is supposed to prevent, not cause. Verify by READING the rendered session-start text, not by counting matches.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-M05", "loud": true, "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/audits/archived-register-readers-fable-probe.md (E11 Fable probe, merged #12681); re-counted independently by session_01XQhayAHWdrSYv8jN54P2HH before filing", "rerun": "grep -oE '(board-pointer|session-board|OPEN-ITEMS|health-review-backlog|performance-review-backlog|ml-review-backlog|research-review-backlog|system-review|delegate-work|MANAGER-LEASE|SESSIONS\\.json|duty)' .claude/settings.json | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; # FINDING STILL APPLIES while this prints any line. Expected clear state: no output."}, "routed_to": "THE OPERATOR, via section 2 of the next daily brief. Not delegable: .claude/ is harness configuration, an agent editing it is refused [Self-Modification], and that refusal is correct and was not worked around. What is needed is either the operator making the edit or an explicit grant naming .claude/settings.json, the way the spawn-provenance grant named manager/SKILL.md.", "state": "done", "terminal_reason": "FIXED 2026-09-21 under operator grant (manager-scope-exception.yaml :: MGR-20260921-STALE-SESSION-HOOKS). Item 0's coordination-board protocol replaced with what is live; /system-review marked retired; the definition of done repointed from the three archived backlogs to the pipeline and checklist; Rule 2's filing target repointed; the delegate-work + session-registry paragraph replaced with the manager contract; the board-nudge PreToolUse hook DELETED since the thing it nudged is gone; the merge-slot guard KEPT but repointed at the per-branch file claim, which is still live and required. VERIFIED rather than assumed: all six hook commands re-parse under `bash -n`, and the rendered session-start text was read back after the edit. NOT YET OBSERVED on a fresh session — the next lane spawned is the first real test, and a successor should say whether its startup text was clean.", "what": "EVERY SESSION IN THIS REPO IS TOLD, BEFORE ITS FIRST TOOL CALL, TO USE FILES THE RESET ARCHIVED. .claude/settings.json's SessionStart, PreToolUse and Stop hooks carry 22 references to archived paths and retired skills -- COUNTED 2026-09-21 by the manager, independently of the report that raised it: session-board x6, board-pointer x6, /system-review x4, health-review-backlog x2, performance-review-backlog, ml-review-backlog, `duty`, `delegate-work`. [!] THIS IS THE MOST EXPENSIVE INSTANCE OF THE ORPHAN CLASS FOUND SO FAR, because it is not a degraded check a session might never run -- it is the FIRST THING EVERY SESSION READS, and it instructs them to register on a coordination board that does not exist and to file findings into backlogs nothing reads. It is a live tax on every lane this manager spawns. [!] IT IS ALSO PLAUSIBLY A CONTRIBUTING CAUSE OF PI-20260921-0004: three of six lanes opened by questioning whether their task was injected, and one named the hook text specifically as part of what made the session look wrong -- a startup block issuing confident instructions about absent files is exactly the shape of a prompt-injection tell. That link is PLAUSIBLE AND NOT ESTABLISHED; the stall reproduced for other reasons too and the hooks were never isolated as a variable. [!] THE OPERATOR MUST DO THIS ONE OR EXPLICITLY GRANT IT. .claude/settings.json is harness configuration and an agent editing it is refused [Self-Modification] -- the manager confirmed that refusal twice today on the adjacent .claude/skills path. The operator's 2026-09-21 grant covered the spawn-provenance fix specifically and is NOT being stretched to cover this: an approval in one context does not extend to the next."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "R1 (the corpus re-run with cost defaults ON) has landed AND the operator has been re-asked R6 with that corpus's verdict in front of them, and has answered. Verified by their recorded answer on the R6 row, not by R1 landing alone — R1 landing is what makes the question ASKABLE, not what answers it.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-M08", "loud": true, "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "operator", "ref": "operator decision 2026-09-21, R6, answered in a four-question popup with the measurement stated", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('docs/claude/work/MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json'));r=[i for i in d['items'] if i['id']=='R1'][0];print('R1 state:',r['state'])\"; # THE DEFERRAL EXPIRES when R1 reaches landed_unproven or done"}, "state": "queued", "what": "R6 IS DEFERRED, NOT SETTLED: 'should the system trade at all right now' was answered 'keep the roster as-is, decide after D1/R1' by the operator on 2026-09-21, with the measurement in front of them — lifetime real-money expectancy -0.3231R over n=431, against a corpus that is fee-only and optimistic by an unknown amount (+0.57R on the one leg anyone checked). [!] THIS ROW EXISTS BECAUSE A DEFERRAL WITH NO DUE CONDITION IS HOW A DECISION GETS SILENTLY SETTLED. 'Decide after X' is precisely the shape the follow-through pipeline was built for: nothing about the answer makes it ask for attention again, and the corpus re-run is days out. Without this row the question quietly becomes 'yes, keep trading', forever, by default and without anyone choosing it. [!] WHEN IT COMES BACK, the question is NOT re-asked cold — it is re-asked WITH the re-run corpus's verdict, which is the whole point of waiting. [!] THE derisk_only MANDATES ARE NOT BLOCKED by this deferral: they read live measurement, not the corpus, and their worst case removes exposure. A leg going net-negative on the mirror can still be pulled meanwhile."}
