{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "A session that was NOT pointed here by its prompt reads the readout line in the CLAUDE.md brief and WRITES AT LEAST ONE TRUE blocked_on edge on a row it actually understands, saying which row and why — i.e. it ACTED on the refusal rather than noting it. ⚠️ RENDERING IS NOT EVIDENCE: that the block appears in CLAUDE.md is a deploy, not an observation — the same distinction that keeps OI-20260826-SESSION-BRIEF-NEVER-READ-BY-A-FRESH-SESSION open. ⚠️ A BULK PASS OVER THE 578 UNASSESSED ROWS DOES NOT CLEAR THIS AND IS A HARM: an invented edge is read by the computation as a true blocker, and a false blocker is worse than a missing one — the work store's README records that exact failure happening on 2026-09-01. ⚠️ COVERAGE RISING WITH NO ATTRIBUTABLE SESSION DOES NOT CLEAR IT EITHER; record WHICH session did it. ⚠️ AND 'a session read it and ignored it' does NOT clear this — that is a different and more useful finding, and belongs in `observation` rather than being treated as a pass.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-12"}, "id": "OI-20260901-CONSTRAINT-READOUT-SHIPPED-AND-IT-REFUSES-NOBODY-HAS-ACTED-ON-THE-REFUSAL", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260901-CONSTRAINT-READOUT-SHIPPED-AND-IT-REFUSES-NOBODY-HAS-ACTED-ON-THE-REFUSAL", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260901-CONSTRAINT-READOUT-SHIPPED-AND-IT-REFUSES-NOBODY-HAS-ACTED-ON-THE-REFUSAL'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] E1/A1 shipped (operating-layer Phase D, PR #10680): scripts/ops/constraint_readout.py computes the constraint over the work store's typed blocked_on edges and renders the four-item readout to docs/claude/READOUT.md, with its headline in the CLAUDE.md session brief under the cycle priority. ⚠️ IT NAMES NO STAGE, and that is the correct output: measured over all 584 objects (0 parse failures), only 6 carry an ASSESSED blocked_on basis — 1.0% against a declared 50% floor — so the verdict is `insufficient_basis`. THE MACHINERY IS BUILT AND THE DIAGNOSIS IS NOT AVAILABLE; those are different facts and only the first shipped. ⚠️ THE RISK THIS ROW WATCHES IS NOT THAT THE READOUT IS WRONG — it is that a permanently-refusing readout gets SKIMMED PAST, becoming one more block in a brief that is supposed to shrink. The design makes two things depend on it (A1 depends on E1; E2 capability build is PULLED by a held-up stage, never self-started) and BOTH are unenforceable while no stage can be named. verified_at is deliberately null: no observation has been made, and dating it today would be a claim of one."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "THREE PARTS, and the first two are different facts. (1) #10679 is approved and merged, or explicitly rejected -- either settles it; being un-actioned does not. (2) A REAL give-up row on the fleet is OBSERVED carrying share_hold=<state> in both the log and the retMsg (/api/diag/journalctl on ict-trader-live.service, or the close_failure page text). A passing unit test is NOT this observation, and neither is reading the merged diff. (3) The live GLD wedge is resolved -- order 2e843e04 gone and the position flat or legitimately closed -- AND the resolution is ATTRIBUTED: operator/venue action, or Alpaca completing its own cancel. [!] If the position simply disappears with no attribution, record THAT rather than clearing on it; an unexplained resolution is not evidence the mechanism works, and this repo has already been bitten by crediting an unrelated repair (see the PROTECTION_REASSERT_MODE row in CLAUDE.md, whose one live exhibit vanished with the cause unestablished). [!] DO NOT CLEAR ON A QUIET BANNER. The close_failure banner clearing means the close stopped being ATTEMPTED (position gone, package closed) -- not that a wedge was handled correctly. [!] AND AS OF 2026-09-02, DO NOT CLEAR ON A QUIET PAGER EITHER (MI-34). The operator chose to DOWNGRADE this class out of the paging channel: a close failure whose share_hold reads broker_cancel_wedged is carried in the rolled-up digest instead of paging, so the pages going quiet is now the DESIGNED behaviour and says NOTHING abou", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-11"}, "id": "OI-20260901-ALPACA-SHARE-HOLD-CLASSIFIER-SHIPPED-NOT-YET-OBSERVED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260901-ALPACA-SHARE-HOLD-CLASSIFIER-SHIPPED-NOT-YET-OBSERVED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260901-ALPACA-SHARE-HOLD-CLASSIFIER-SHIPPED-NOT-YET-OBSERVED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] PR #10679 (DRAFT, Tier-2 order path, awaiting operator approval) adds classify_share_hold() so an Alpaca close that cannot free its shares says WHY -- four never-collapsed states, of which broker_cancel_wedged means no retry will ever work -- and makes _cancel_open_orders_detailed read the broker's cancel response instead of discarding it. [!] THIS ROW READ 'NOT MERGED AND NOT OBSERVED' UNTIL 2026-09-02 AND THE FIRST HALF IS NOW FALSE -- do not re-quote it. Commit 839247cc IS on origin/main and classify_share_hold() is in the tree (verified by `git merge-base --is-ancestor` and by grepping origin/main, not by reading a PR page). The SECOND half is untouched and is what this row is now for: NOTHING HAS BEEN SEEN emitting a share_hold state on the fleet. Merged is not deployed and deployed is not observed; the two gaps were always separate and only one closed. [!] THIS IS ALSO THE STANDING RECORD THAT THE LIVE WEDGE IS UNRESOLVED. alpaca_paper GLD (39 shares, pkg-6a8e3fb325464be3) could not close as of 2026-09-01T21:20Z because OCO parent 2e843e04-5487-470c-a702-70e796fbd05e has sat at status 'pending_cancel' with canceled_at null since 2026-08-27. [!] CORRECTED 2026-09-12 by session_013iSqp4LsU1eq8K326eUtgj (MI-279 OPS lane, U5) -- THAT STATUS IS NO LONGER TRUE AND THIS ROW'S OWN `observation` ALREADY SAID SO, so the row contradicted itself and a session reading the summary first would carry the wrong venue state. MEASURED on /api/diag/log_file?name=close_wedge_standing, updated_at 2026-09-12T14:48:34Z: 2e843e04-5487-470c-a702-70e796fbd05e is `still new` and 891ddff0-b24d-4039-9322-8492bcd51e66 is `still held` -- NOT pending_cancel, and `canceled_at` is null on both. So the broker is not even CLAIMING to cancel, which is a different