{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 2, "clears_when": "BOTH, and they are different facts — say which you cleared rather than clearing on the easier one. (1) MERGED AND DEPLOYED: PR #11037 merges with the back-fill question answered ON THE RECORD either way, and `/api/diag/version` reads a `git_sha` at or after that merge — a merge is not a deploy. (2) OBSERVED ON THE FLEET: a trade that CLOSES AFTER that deploy, having been held longer than 14 days, is found either carrying a pnl or carrying `pnl_source` — read from trade_journal.db::trades, naming the trade. ⚠️ (2) SAYS *CLOSES AFTER*, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE CRITERION: a long-held row that closed BEFORE the deploy satisfies the wording on its face while being one of the 5 back-filled rows, which proves the back-fill happened and NOT that forward behaviour is correct. ⚠️ EXPLICITLY NOT SUFFICIENT: the PR merging (that is (1) only); CI green or the 312 tests passing (a harness cannot reach the fleet, and this repo has paid for that distinction repeatedly); the silent-row count falling (see probe_absent_reason — it falls on its own); or the absence of an alarm, since the defect's entire signature is silence. ⚠️ IF THE OPERATOR DECLINES THE MERGE, this row does NOT clear — it CHANGES: long-held closes then remain permanently unpriceable AND undeclarable, which is a legitimate decision and must be RECORDED as one with that consequence stated, rather than left looking like work in flight.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": null}, "id": "OI-20260905-MI-128-SWEEP-WINDOW-REKEYED-AND-THE-PR-HOLDS-ON-A-BACKFILL-DECISION", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260905-MI-128-SWEEP-WINDOW-REKEYED-AND-THE-PR-HOLDS-ON-A-BACKFILL-DECISION", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dump