{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, and they are different facts -- say WHICH you cleared rather than clearing the row on the easier one.\n(1) The consumer is OBSERVED RUNNING on the fleet: at least one row in runtime_logs/ict_scalp_exit_head_soak.jsonl (/api/diag/log_file?name=ict_scalp_exit_head_soak), read from the LIVE VM, carrying mode=annotate. ⚠️ A passing unit test is NOT this observation and neither is reading the merged diff -- 93 assertions pass in tests/test_exit_head_apply_parity.py + tests/test_ict_scalp_exit_head_consumer.py and a harness cannot reach the VM. Expect decision_state=not_scored on every row; that CONFIRMS the tf guard is refusing correctly and is the clause-(1) evidence, not a failure.\n(2) The ARTIFACT gap is dispositioned -- either a 5m/15m ict_scalp exit-head artifact is published to the mirror and observed admitting a leg (a soak row with decision_state != not_scored and a non-null model_id), OR the operator decides no scalp head will be trained, which is a legitimate outcome and must be RECORDED as a decision rather than left looking like a soak about to start. ⚠️ DO NOT CLEAR (2) ON A QUIET LOG: an all-not_scored file is the EXPECTED state and says nothing about whether anyone intends to train the head.\n⚠️ THIS ROW DOES NOT TRACK ARMING. Arming is Tier-3, runs into the 2026-08-23 SHIP BLOCKED decision above, and needs fresh evidence that survives re-partitioning -- not a wiring fix.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-17"}, "id": "OI-20260906-ICT-SCALP-EXIT-HEAD-CONSUMER-SHIPPED-AND-CANNOT-SCORE-UNTIL-A-SCALP-HEAD-IS-PUBLISHED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260906-ICT-SCALP-EXIT-HEAD-CONSUMER-SHIPPED-AND-CANNOT-SCORE-UNTIL-A-SCALP-HEAD-IS-PUBLISHED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items