{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 2, "clears_when": "THREE PARTS, and they are different facts — say WHICH you cleared rather than clearing the row on the easiest. (1) THE ROOT CAUSE LANDS: _bybit_position_protection selects the book instead of taking rows[0], AND its two collapses are separated — `not rows` on a symbol-scoped call returns None (we could not look) rather than _flat, and more than one LIVE book returns None rather than picking one. (2) THE FIX IS OBSERVED ON THE FLEET, which is a DIFFERENT fact from (1): a netting_attribution_soak row on a hedge-armed symbol carrying a non-zero exchange_qty where the venue holds a position, AND no further netting_attributed -> same-size-adopt pair. [!] A PASSING UNIT TEST CLEARS NEITHER — a fixture cannot reproduce which row Bybit lists first, which is the whole mechanism. [!] AND THE ABSENCE OF NEW ADOPT PAIRS IS NOT SUFFICIENT ALONE: the flap needs a second live position in the sibling book to arise at all, so a quiet week may mean the condition did not occur rather than that it is fixed. Say which you established. (3) THE NINE UNGRADEABLE FLAT READS ARE GRADED, or the soak is given `source` + `position_idx` so they become gradeable and the count is recorded. That count is what a NETTING_ATTRIBUTION_MODE widening decision actually rests on and nobody has it. [!] THE OPEN ETHUSDT POSITION CLOSING DOES NOT CLEAR ANY PART OF THIS. It will close eventually by TP, SL or a strategy exit, and that says nothing about the reconciler. If it closes with an UNEXPLAINED resolution, record ", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-12"}, "id": "OI-20260908-A-HEDGE-BOOK-FLAT-READ-IS-CLOSING-LIVE-BYBIT-POSITIONS-AND-THE-FLAP-GUARD-CANNOT-SEE-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260908-A-HEDGE-BOOK-FLAT-READ-IS-CLOSING-LIVE-BYBIT-POSITIONS-AND-THE-FLAP-GUARD-CANNOT-SEE-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260908-A-HEDGE-BOOK-FLAT-READ-IS-CLOSING-LIVE-BYBIT-POSITIONS-AND-THE-FLAP-GUARD-CANNOT-SEE-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] The netting reconciler is closing LIVE Bybit positions because it grades a symbol off get_positions rows[0] and a hedge book reads flat — three provable false closes, one open right now, and real money is in the exposed population"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "BOTH, and they are different facts. (a) A run of e35-bracket-sweep.yml with only=qld_trend_long_1d,tqqq_trend_long_1d completes ON A RUNNER with both legs SCHEDULED (not refused) and its own fetch step reporting a non-trivial row count for each — read the run log, never the workflow file, and record the feed_source the planner emitted. ⚠️ A GREEN RUN WITH BOTH LEGS REFUSED CLEARS NOTHING and is the failure being watched; so does an empty `legs` list, which the sweep exits 0 on (BL-20260826-E35-RUNNER-WRITES-A-FILENAME-THE-SWEEP-NEVER-READS). ⚠️ The planner selftest passing clears nothing either — 66 assertions pass in a harness and a harness cannot reach a runner. (b) The operator decides on § 6: either tp_intent moves to mode: none with a reason naming the measured reachability ceiling (NOT the trail_is_the_profit_exit the other 20 legs carry, which would lose exactly the fact this cost a session to buy), or they decide to leave it — which is legitimate and must be RECORDED as a decision rather than left looking like an edit about to happen. ⚠️ IF THE RUNNER RUN DISAGREES WITH THE LOCAL ONE, that does NOT clear this row and is the more valuable finding — the two substrates differ (Yahoo direct vs the fetcher) and a divergence would say the positive control was not sufficient. Write it into observation and keep the row open.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-08"}, "id": "OI-20260908-QLD-TQQQ-EXAMINED-LOCALLY-AND-THE-CI-FEED-PATH-HAS-NEVER-RUN", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260908-QLD-TQQQ-EXAMINED-LOCALLY-AND-THE-CI-FEED-PATH-HAS-NEVER-RUN", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260908-QLD-TQQQ-