{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "BOTH halves, and they are different facts — say WHICH you cleared. (a) A caller of /api/bot/trades/closed can tell a WINDOW from a POPULATION without already knowing the answer (per BL-20260908-INCLUDE-PAPER-TRUE-NARROWS-THE-REAL-MONEY-POPULATION-AND-A-SESSION-REPORTED-15-FOR-447's criteria). (b) The disagreement count printed by scripts/research/real_money_close_attribution.py falls to 0, or the route publishes the raw exit_reason beside closeReason. ⚠️ DO NOT CLEAR THIS BECAUSE A SESSION READ IT — the point is the API, not the reader. ⚠️ AND DO NOT CLEAR IT ON A DOC EDIT ALONE: documenting the trap in bot-api-reference.md satisfies the MINIMUM fallback of (a) and nothing of (b).", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-12"}, "id": "OI-20260908-THE-REAL-MONEY-CLOSED-POPULATION-IS-447-NOT-15-AND-TWO-SURFACES-DISAGREE-ON-ITS-EXIT-LABELS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260908-THE-REAL-MONEY-CLOSED-POPULATION-IS-447-NOT-15-AND-TWO-SURFACES-DISAGREE-ON-ITS-EXIT-LABELS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260908-THE-REAL-MONEY-CLOSED-POPULATION-IS-447-NOT-15-AND-TWO-SURFACES-DISAGREE-ON-ITS-EXIT-LABELS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] TWO MEASUREMENT TRAPS ON THE REAL-MONEY TRADE SURFACE, both of which have ALREADY produced a wrong operator-facing conclusion (2026-09-08, MI-200). Read this BEFORE measuring real-money performance. (1) THE POPULATION. GET /api/bot/trades/closed takes include_paper, DEFAULT False, so the default response is ALREADY real-money-only. Passing include_paper=true and then filtering to accountClass=='real_money' does NOT widen the real-money set — it NARROWS it to whatever fraction of the newest `limit` MIXED rows happens to be real money. Measured: ?limit=200 -> 200 real-money rows; ?limit=200&include_paper=true -> 15 real-money rows; paged to exhaustion -> 447, window 2026-05-09..2026-09-04. A dispatch reported the 15 as 'the real-money population' and concluded '0 wins, 13 losses'. The book is actually 117 W / 258 L / 49 flat (n=424 graded). The failure is SILENT: 200 OK, every row genuinely real money, nothing says the set was truncated. (2) THE LABEL. `closeReason` on that route folds FIFTEEN distinct mechanisms into `other`, including 182 rows that ARE strategy exits (vwap_cross, sl_cross, tp_cross, exit_head, time_decay, stale_stop). Reading `other` as 'not a strategy exit' is wrong in BOTH directions. /api/bot/strategies uses a DIFFERENT taxonomy over the SAME column and the two disagree on 174 of 447 rows (38.9%); 53 rows read `sl` on one surface and `other` on the other. Read RAW trades.exit_reason, never closeReason, to answer 'did the strategy's exit fire?'."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 2, "clears_when": "BOTH, and they are different facts — say WHICH you cleared rather than clearing the row on the easier one. (1) SUPPRESSION OBSERVED: after a full cooldown window has elapsed past the stamp, /api/diag/log_file?name=prop_status_request shows breakout_1's `last_request` UNCHANGED while the account is flat, i.e. the ask did not fire. [!] THIS REQUIRES A POSITIVE CONTROL AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL: silence alone is also what a crashed import looks like. Once #11546 is deployed the control is in the SAME file — `last_verdict: quiescent` with a `last_assessed_at` inside the window proves the module ran and chose not to ask. BEFORE #11546 there is no such control and clause (1) CANNOT be cleared honestly; do not clear it on the stamp alone. (2) THE ASK STILL FIRES WHEN IT SHOULD: an ask is observed for a real trigger — an open prop position, a real (non-suppressed) ticket after the snapshot, or an unreadable read. A change that silences EVERYTHING is a regression that looks identical to success on clause (1), and this clause is the only thing separating them. [!] IF THE OPERATOR IS PINGED ABOUT A QUIESCENT ACCOUNT AFTER THE DEPLOY, that does NOT clear this row and is the more valuable finding — write it into observation and keep the row open. [!] IF THE OPERATOR DECIDES the wall-clock ask should return, this row does NOT clear — it CHANGES: that is a legitimate Tier-2 decision and must be RECORDED as one rather than left looking like an observation about to happen.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-12"}, "id": "OI-20260909-PROP-STATUS-REQUEST-TRIGGER-DEPLOYED-BUT-THE-SUPPRESSION-HAS-NEVER-BEEN-OBSERVED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260909-PROP-STATUS-REQUEST-TRIGGER-DEPLOYED-BUT-THE-SUPPRESSION-HAS-NEVER-BEEN-OBSERVED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-