{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "TWO CLAUSES NOW, AND THEY ARE DIFFERENT FACTS - say WHICH you cleared rather than clearing the row on the easier one. (1) DISPOSITION: each of the six carries a RECORDED operator disposition - approved, rejected, or deferred-with-a-reason - written into the backlog row it corresponds to. THIS CLAUSE IS MET as of 2026-09-09T23:5xZ; see the observation for the six row ids. It is kept in the text rather than deleted so a reader can see what was asked and what discharged it. (2) CARRIAGE: every APPROVED proposal is either BUILT-AND-OBSERVED on the fleet, or carried by its own named row that a session will read without this one. Clause (2) was ADDED 2026-09-09 when clause (1) was met with four of six unbuilt - because a row that discharged there would vacate the session brief for precisely the work it exists to stop losing, which is the audit's own 'do X first so we can scope Y' finding applied to this row. PARTIAL PROGRESS DOES NOT CLEAR THIS ROW: say WHICH of the six are carried and leave it open while any is neither built nor carried. AN APPROVAL IS NOT A BUILD, A MERGE IS NOT A DEPLOY, AND A DEPLOY IS NOT AN OBSERVATION - F-36 is merged and has never run on a live reduce, which is exactly the state clause (2) refuses to accept as done. THE AUDIT REPORT BEING PUBLISHED CLEARS NOTHING - the report existed on 2026-09-09 and that is the state this row describes, not its resolution. A FINDING BEING FIXED BY A LATER SESSION THAT NEVER SAW THIS AUDIT STILL COUNTS - record it, because", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-12"}, "id": "OI-20260909-THE-FULL-SYSTEM-AUDITS-TIER-2-AND-TIER-3-PROPOSALS-ARE-FILED-AND-CARRIED-BY-NOTHING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260909-THE-FULL-SYSTEM-AUDITS-TIER-2-AND-TIER-3-PROPOSALS-ARE-FILED-AND-CARRIED-BY-NOTHING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260909-THE-FULL-SYSTEM-AUDITS-TIER-2-AND-TIER-3-PROPOSALS-ARE-FILED-AND-CARRIED-BY-NOTHING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] MI-225's audit produced 6 money-at-risk proposals the operator must decide, and the audit completing hands them to nobody"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "EITHER of two OPPOSITE outcomes, and they are different findings -- say which. (a) THE DROP IS REAL: at least one position_read_state_soak row carries dropped_symbol_dedupe_count >= 1, read off /api/diag/log_file, naming the symbol and the position_idx of the book that was discarded. That is the live-money case -- a second book on a symbol already emitted, invisible to every caller keyed on (symbol, side), which is what gates the close decision at order_monitor.py:4348 -- and it is the EVIDENCE a Tier-3 behaviour-change proposal would rest on. The manager, not this row, puts that to the operator. (b) THE DROP DOES NOT HAPPEN HERE: rows accrue across at least 3 distinct UTC days with dropped_symbol_dedupe_count == 0 throughout AND a non-zero denominator (rows_seen > 0 on those rows, so the reader was genuinely looking). That RETIRES the Tier-3 proposal on this account set and must be RECORDED as that decision rather than left looking like a soak still running. !! AN EMPTY LOG CLEARS NEITHER AND IS ITSELF THE FINDING: zero rows after a full cadence means the writer is not writing or the code is not deployed -- a deploy defect, not a quiet book. Zero rows and 'rows accruing with no drops' are OPPOSITE facts and must never both be reported as 'the soak is quiet'. !! A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING: 13 tests pass in a harness and a harness cannot reach a venue. !! AND MERGING CLEARS NOTHING -- a merge is not a deploy and a deploy is not a row.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-17"}, "id": "OI-20260909-POSITION-READ-STATE-SOAK-DECIDES-WHETHER-THE-COLLAPSED-READ-EVER-FIRES", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260909-POSITION-READ-STATE-SOAK-DECIDES-WHETHER-THE-COLLAPSED-READ-EVER-FIRES", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-IT