{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "A PLANTED VIOLATION IS OBSERVED BEING REPORTED, end to end on the fleet -- a row on /api/diag/log_file?name=invariant_violations AND the matching Level.ERROR reaching the operator. !! A CONTINUED ZERO CLEARS NOTHING, and that is this row's whole point: the previous 14.7-day zero was produced by an instrument that could not report a violation at all, so 'still zero' is exactly what the broken state looked like. !! A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING -- a harness cannot reach a failed exchange read on a live account, which IS the finding. !! MERGING CLEARS NOTHING: a merge is not a deploy and a deploy is not a row. !! `controls_ok: true` ON THE SOAK CLEARS NOTHING EITHER, and it will read true from the very first pass: it grades three PLANTED inputs through the deployed classifier and reaches no venue, no account resolver, no DB row and no alert path -- which is why it ships beside controls_scope: 'pure_classifier_only'. Quoting it as end-to-end evidence is the exact misreading that label exists to prevent. !! THE FIRST INTERPRETABLE READ IS THE DENOMINATOR, NOT THE FINDING: read /api/diag/log_file?name=closed_flat_coverage and establish rows exist AT ALL with examined > 0. Zero rows after a full tick cadence means the writer is not writing or the code is not deployed -- a DEPLOY DEFECT, the opposite fact from a quiet book, and it must never be reported as 'no violations observed'. Then read state_counts.could_not_look and cadence_basis BESIDE any zero: a zero over an unread book", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-17"}, "id": "OI-20260909-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-CAN-FINALLY-SPEAK-AND-HAS-NOT-YET-SPOKEN", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260909-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-CAN-FINALLY-SPEAK-AND-HAS-NOT-YET-SPOKEN", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260909-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-CAN-FINALLY-SPEAK-AND-HAS-NOT-YET-SPOKEN'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] The closed->exchange-flat invariant -- THE ONE MECHANISM that can independently contradict 'this trade is closed' -- was silent for four independent reasons, each alone sufficient, and its 14.7-day zero-violation record was evidence of nothing. Audit F-11 (a failed exchange read graded FLAT at 5 of 5 early-return sites, so the falsifier was cleared by exactly the condition it exists to catch), F-12 (a 60s lookback against a measured >=101.9s invocation period, leaving >=41% of every period examined by nobody, BY ARITHMETIC not by failure), F-13 (invariant_violations.jsonl on no diag allowlist, alert at Level.WARN which outcomes.py excludes from Telegram). Operator approved all three, Tier-2, 2026-09-09 (chosen: all_three on WO-20260909-DECISION-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-CANNOT-SEE-A-FAILED-READ). Built as MI-228, PR #11603. !! A FOURTH BLINDNESS WAS FOUND WHILE BUILDING THE FIX AND IT SUBSUMES THE OTHER THREE AS AN EXPLANATION OF THE ZERO: the position size was read from qty/contracts, and clients.py::account_open_positions normalises all 4 of 4 venue branches to `size`, so float(None or None or 0) == 0.0 and A LIVE RESIDUAL GRADED FLAT ON EVERY ACCOUNT from the module's first commit. The zero was GUARANTEED BY CONSTRUCTION, not merely uninformative. Every fixture in tests/test_closed_flat_invariant.py uses `qty`, so 15 tests were green throughout while exercising a shape production never produces. !! NOTHING HERE TOUCHES AN ORDER PATH -- the check is alert-only and stays that way; the operator's answer records that a falsifier which can finally speak is an INPUT to a decision, never the decision."}
