{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "A RENDER PRODUCED BY THE CRON, WITH A TOKEN, IS OBSERVED GRADING IT -- i.e. docs/claude/DUE.json on `main` carries a `red_main_runs` entry whose `state` is `read`, and EITHER it names at least one workflow (the source found a positive) OR it reports zero rows, which is then a genuine clean negative because the token half is established by the entry existing at all. Record WHICH, and the run that produced it. !! `red_main_runs` STILL ABSENT FROM THE sources ENVELOPE DOES NOT CLEAR THIS AND IS ITSELF THE FINDING: absent means collect() never called it, which is a wiring defect, and it is a DIFFERENT fact from `could_not_read`, which means it was called and had no token. !! A `could_not_read` ENTRY CLEARS NOTHING EITHER -- that is the source correctly saying it could not look, and a due-list that renders it forever is a source deployed into a workflow that cannot feed it. !! THE MERGE CLEARS NOTHING: a merge is not a deploy and a deploy is not a run, and 4f3e0c388 is what OPENED this row. !! A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING: 17 tests pass in a harness and a harness cannot reach api.github.com -- which is the whole reason this row exists rather than a line in the PR body. !! AND IF THE FIRST REAL RUN NAMES A WORKFLOW THAT IS RED ON THE DEFAULT BRANCH, that is not a defect in this source: it is the condition it was built to route, and the row clears on the OBSERVATION while the red itself becomes somebody's work.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-17"}, "id": "OI-20260913-THE-DEFAULT-BRANCH-RED-READER-IS-DEPLOYED-AND-HAS-NEVER-QUERIED-THE-ACTIONS-API", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260913-THE-DEFAULT-BRANCH-RED-READER-IS-DEPLOYED-AND-HAS-NEVER-QUERIED-THE-ACTIONS-API", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260913-THE-DEFAULT-BRANCH-RED-READER-IS-DEPLOYED-AND-HAS-NEVER-QUERIED-THE-ACTIONS-API'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "scripts/ops/render_due_list.py gained `src_red_main_runs` (MI-280 U90 lane, PR #12209, merged 4f3e0c388): the latest COMPLETED push-to-`main` run of each workflow whose conclusion is a real failure, rendered on docs/claude/DUE.md. It exists because `src_red_crons` queries `?event=schedule` and nothing else, so a red on the DEFAULT BRANCH was read by no source at all -- measured: `main` at 2a6c1b24d genuinely carried a duplicated register id, check_register_ids.py exits 1 at that commit with no --base needed, guards.yml carries `push: branches: [main]` with register-id-guard always-on, and the duplicate was nonetheless found by an unrelated PR author tripping over it. !! IT HAS NEVER RUN AGAINST THE REAL ACTIONS API. Its only caller is .github/workflows/due-list.yml on a `50 5 * * *` cron, and it needs a GITHUB_TOKEN; tokenless it returns `could_not_read` by design. 17 tests pass and a harness cannot reach api.github.com."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "THE INSTRUMENT IS RE-RUN ON OR AFTER THE DATED THRESHOLD AND RETURNS A GRADED VERDICT -- `fall_persists` or `fall_vanished` -- with the era arms reported SEPARATELY and the population stated. The dates are 2026-09-28 (share arm) and 2026-10-01 (winner-R arm); they are DIFFERENT arms reaching n at DIFFERENT times, so say WHICH one you graded rather than clearing the row on the earlier one. [!] TIME PASSING CLEARS NOTHING. The dates are a projection from the MEASURED arrival rate of netting_attributed closes, and that rate is itself what the fixes are supposed to have changed -- so if the fixes worked, n arrives LATER than projected, and the row's own prediction is self-defeating in the reassuring direction. Re-read the counts; do not read the calendar. [!] A POOLED 3+4 RESULT DOES NOT CLEAR THIS unless the report says in terms that it attributes to NEITHER fix. That is the trap this unit already fell into and labelled. [!] AND THE SCOPING RULE MUST BE THE STAMP-AND-SOAK UNION (U49's correction), not `exit_reason` alone. A verdict graded on the cheaper filter is graded on a biased, incomplete population -- 7 of 33 applied soak rows missing, unevenly across eras, and the MEASURED rows preferentially dropped -- and must be recorded as `unmeasurable`, never as a result. [!] IF THE OPERATOR DECIDES the question is not worth waiting for, this row does NOT clear -- it CHANGES: the netting fixes are then declared unverified by choice, which is a legitimate decision and must be RECORDE", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-17"}, "id": "OI-20260917-THE-NETTING-POST-FIX-REMEASURE-IS-RUNNABLE-AND-UNDER-POWERED-AND-ITS-N-ARRIVES-ON-A-DATE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260917-THE-NETTING-POST-FIX-REMEASURE-IS-RUNNABLE-AND-UNDER-POWERED-AND-ITS-N-ARRIVES-ON-A-DATE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260917-THE-NETTING-POST-FIX-REMEASURE-IS-RUNNABLE-AND-UNDER-POWERED-AND-ITS-N-ARRIVES-ON-A-DATE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "MI-278 U52 built the instrument BL-20260912-THE-NETTING-ATTRIBUTED-PATH-CARRIES-THE-LARGEST-SHARE-OF-THE-WINNER-COLLAPSE-AND-IS-100-PERCENT-ESTIMATED asks for (scripts/research/netting_postfix_remeasure.py, 54 self-test controls, 14 planted defects all caught) and RAN it. Option (a) -- re-measure after the hedge-book fix -- is reachable at last, because 46e1efb1f is on main (verified against the commit object, NOT against prose claiming it). IT RETURNS `insufficient_n`, AND THAT IS THE DELIVERABLE: 4 graded post-fix winners against a required 11 (two-proportion, alpha 0.05, power 0.80). Converted to DATES at the measured arrival rate: the share arm reaches n around 2026-09-28, the winner-R arm around 2026-10-01. THIS ROW EXISTS BECAUSE OF THE STANDING OPERATOR RULE that anything soaking is logged with a timer or a soak threshold, so somebody comes back when the soak is ready -- without it the n accrues and nobody returns, which is how a held question becomes an abandoned one. [!] THREE THINGS A SUCCESSOR MUST NOT RE-DERIVE. (1) THERE ARE TWO FIXES IN THE WINDOW, so there are FOUR eras, not two: #11435 (2026-09-08) and #11903 (2026-09-12). Only the POOLED 3+4 arm reaches p<0.10, and a pooled arm ATTRIBUTES TO NEITHER FIX -- the instrument labels it POOLED_3+4 for exactly that reason. Five contrasts, Bonferroni alpha 0.0100, NONE survives. (2) THE SCOPING RULE DECIDES THE VERDICT: `exit_reason` alone gives pooled p=0.0375 (significant); U49's corrected stamp-AND-soak union gives p=0.0681 (not). The cheaper filter misses 7 of 33 applied soak rows and misses them UNEVENLY across eras (4/2/1). (3) THE UNSOUND SCOPE IS BIASED TOWARD `estimated`: 2 of 39 rows are MEASURED and BOTH arrive via notes_stamp, because a row the exit_reason filter misses closes under sl_cross and so gets broker truth. Boundary invariance was MEASURED not assumed -- zero rows fall in either merge->git-sync window, so no era assignment turns on the +/-5-minute deploy estimate. Era census on the 1000-row journal tail: pre-e35 164 closed / 13 netting / 7.9%; e35-only 162 / 18 / 11.1%; fix-A 79 / 5 / 6.3%; fix-A+B 72 / 3 / 4.2%. Memo: docs/research/m20-u52-the-netting-remeasure-is-runnable-and-under-powered-2026-09-17.md (PR #12439)."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "A REAL automation run is OBSERVED emitting `refreshed_after_generated_conflict` and its PR is then MERGED -- read the run log or the resulting merge, never the branch's existence. Say WHICH run. [!] MERGING #12472 CLEARS NOTHING: a merge is not a deploy of a composite action and a deploy is not a firing, which is the distinction that keeps half the rows in this file open. [!] A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING: 24 tests pass in tests/test_commit_to_main_callers.py and 6 of 6 realistic mutations are caught, and a harness cannot reach a runner -- which is precisely why this row exists beside a green PR. [!] NOR DOES THE REPLAY, however many branches it resolved: it is the strongest available OFFLINE evidence and it is offline, and reporting 30-of-33 as a fleet observation would be exactly the merged-is-not-observed error this register exists to stop. [!] AND THE OPEN-PR COUNT FALLING IS NOT EVIDENCE EITHER, which is the likeliest misread: stale-automation-sweep closes stranded automation PRs, so the pile can shrink for a reason that has nothing to do with this change. Read the state token, not the count. [!] IF A RUN EMITS `failed_conflict_rederive`, that does NOT clear this row and is the MORE VALUABLE finding -- a caller's declared refresh-command does not reproduce its artifact on a runner, which the replay cannot detect. Write it into observation and keep the row open.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-17"}, "id": "OI-20260917-THE-GENERATED-CONFLICT-RECOMPUTE-IS-PROVEN-IN-REPLAY-AND-HAS-NEVER-RUN-ON-A-RUNNER", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260917-THE-GENERATED-CONFLICT-RECOMPUTE-IS-PROVEN-IN-REPLAY-AND-HAS-NEVER-RUN-ON-A-RUNNER", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260917-THE-GENERATED-CONFLICT-RECOMPUTE-IS-PROVEN-IN-REPLAY-AND-HAS-NEVER-RUN-ON-A-RUNNER'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] PR #12472 makes commit-to-main RECOMPUTE a generated artifact on conflict instead of aborting, under three ANDed conditions (a refresh-command is declared; EVERY conflicted path is one the caller named in paths:; the recompute exits 0). MEASURED 2026-09-17 over the COMPLETE population of 70 open PRs at origin/main 19e59662, with both controls passing: 56 of 70 (80.0%) were merge-conflicted, 44 of them automation/** -- this action's OWN PRs -- and the blocked paths were led by GENERATED files (DUE.json/DUE.md in 28, ERROR-FEED-DIGEST.json/.md in 23), with 23 error-feed-digest PRs stacked since 2026-09-13. [!] IT IS PROVEN IN REPLAY AND HAS NEVER RUN ON A RUNNER, AND THOSE ARE DIFFERENT FACTS. The replay took the 33 REAL stranded automation branches on origin, reproduced git merge origin/main, applied the resolution and re-probed: 30 CONFLICT -> CLEAN, 3 correctly refused. That exercises the DECISION and the git mechanics; it does NOT exercise the action's shell on a runner, the bash -c of a caller's refresh-command in the Actions environment, or the push-and-extend-deadline path. [!] AND IT IS NOT MERGED: Tier-1 but landing: hold / changes_landing_machinery per R12, so it cannot self-land and waits on a human merge click."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "ALL THREE decisions in section 4 of the packet are RECORDED -- taken, rejected, or explicitly deferred with a reason -- and a decision to change NOTHING clears a row exactly as legitimately as a change does. (1) The ict_scalp family's tp_at_r (Tier-3; 7 live legs, n=557-1,664 each). (2) TP_VENUE_CAP_PCT: leave it, DECLARE it, or set it per leg -- and note the 'declare' half is TIER-1 and is the only item in the packet with no counter-argument, since 22 legs carry tp_intent mode `none` (20 with reason `trail_is_the_profit_exit`) which is not accurate as stated. (3) Whether fade_breakout_4h and ict_scalp_mgc_15m should be measured at all -- one resolver branch and one feed question. [!] THE PACKET MERGING CLEARS NOTHING. That is what OPENED this row, not what closes it -- the same distinction that keeps OI-20260826-SESSION-BRIEF-NEVER-READ-BY-A-FRESH-SESSION open. [!] RE-RUNNING THE INSTRUMENT CLEARS NOTHING AND IS A HARM: MI-307's memo records that re-measuring is the failure mode OI-20260906 exists to stop -- the diagnosis was established seven times before it was built once. If you re-run it and the numbers hold, that is not progress; write what you saw and leave the row open. [!] A PARTIAL ANSWER DOES NOT CLEAR IT -- say WHICH of the three was decided and leave the row open on the rest. [!] AND IF THE OPERATOR DECIDES the scalp target question is not worth answering, this row does NOT clear -- it CHANGES: the family's target is then knowingly left at a value chosen against ", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-18"}, "id": "OI-20260918-THE-TARGET-GEOMETRY-PACKET-EXISTS-AND-ITS-THREE-DECISIONS-ARE-UNANSWERED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260918-THE-TARGET-GEOMETRY-PACKET-EXISTS-AND-ITS-THREE-DECISIONS-ARE-UNANSWERED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260918-THE-TARGET-GEOMETRY-PACKET-EXISTS-AND-ITS-THREE-DECISIONS-ARE-UNANSWERED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] MI-317 (PR #12526) delivered the per-leg target-geometry decision packet over ALL 55 legs in config/strategies.yaml: docs/research/per-leg-target-geometry-packet-2026-09-18.md and docs/research/mi317-target-geometry-packet-2026-09-18.json, built by scripts/research/mi317_target_geometry_packet.py. It is clause (2) of OI-20260906-THE-BRACKET-CALIBRATION-INSTRUMENT-EXISTS-AND-ITS-VERDICT-HAS-NOT-BEEN-ACTED-ON, and it PROPOSES ONLY -- config/ is untouched and every tp_r and tp_at_r is Tier-3. THE PACKET'S SHAPE: a per-leg number is OWED on 8 legs, is ALREADY IN CONFIG on 10, is REFUSED BY EVIDENCE on 31, and is UNKNOWN on 6. [!] 44 OF THE 55 LEGS DO NOT SET THEIR OWN TARGET -- TP_VENUE_CAP_PCT=0.099 does, one fleet-wide constant named for a Bybit venue boundary -- and 26 OF THOSE 44 TOUCH NO BYBIT ACCOUNT, five routing REAL MONEY through alpaca_live (tlt_pullback_1h, tlt_pullback_1d, ief_pullback_1d, slv_pullback_1d, iaum_pullback_1d). [!] THE OPEN DECISION IS 8 LEGS WIDE AND NONE OF THE EIGHT PLACES A REAL-MONEY ORDER TODAY: the 7 ict_scalp legs route to bybit_1 (paper) and fvg_range_15m is execution: shadow despite its bybit_2 roster line. So this row is NOT money-at-risk; it is a decision that goes stale and gets re-derived if nobody answers it, which is the failure the packet exists to end. [!] DO NOT READ 'refused by evidence on 31' AS 'nobody looked': those 31 were swept at ~180 tp_r cells each and produced ZERO survivors, so their declared value stands BY EVIDENCE. The 6 UNKNOWN legs are the ones nobody looked at, and they are a separate bucket on purpose."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, and they are different facts -- say WHICH you cleared rather than clearing the row on the easier one. (1) THE REPAIR IS OBSERVED ON THE FLEET: a work_decision_sweep_receipt row carries prompted_choice >= 1 or prompted_choice_shortened >= 1 for one of the four named requests, read off /api/diag/log_file?name=work_decision_sweep_receipt AFTER the trader/bot has restarted onto the merge commit. (2) THE OPERATOR CONFIRMS A DECISION PROMPT ARRIVED, naming which question and which conversation. [!] (1) WITHOUT (2) CLEARS HALF: `prompted_choice` means the sweep's sender returned a CONFIRMED send, which is a claim about the CALL, and this repo's own record on OI-20260901-CLAUDE-CHANNEL-SEPARATION is that pings have been 'delivered' to the wrong chat while the operator watched the right one and correctly reported nothing arrived. [!] A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING, and the repo says so in terms: 193 tests pass and 7 planted defects are each caught, and a harness cannot reach a Telegram chat -- which is the whole of what was failing. [!] THE MERGE CLEARS NOTHING: a merge is not a deploy and a deploy is not a delivery. [!] A QUIET RECEIPT CLEARS NOTHING AND IS THE LIKELIEST READING TO GET WRONG: `candidates: 0` is the EMPTY-DENOMINATOR state and says NOTHING about whether a send would have worked -- read `candidates` BEFORE reading any zero in `failed`, and note the four named requests stay candidates until they are either delivered or ANSWERED, so a sudden zero may mean t", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": null}, "id": "OI-20260918-THE-DECISION-CHANNEL-IS-REPAIRED-AND-NO-PROMPT-HAS-BEEN-OBSERVED-ARRIVING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json#OI-20260918-THE-DECISION-CHANNEL-IS-REPAIRED-AND-NO-PROMPT-HAS-BEEN-OBSERVED-ARRIVING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/OPEN-ITEMS.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='OI-20260918-THE-DECISION-CHANNEL-IS-REPAIRED-AND-NO-PROMPT-HAS-BEEN-OBSERVED-ARRIVING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[LOUD] [NEVER VERIFIED] MI-303. THE CAUSE OF THE DEAD DECISION CHANNEL IS FOUND, MEASURED AND REPAIRED, AND NOT ONE PROMPT HAS BEEN OBSERVED ARRIVING SINCE -- those are different facts and only the first holds. Telegram caps sendMessage's text at 4096 CHARACTERS and render_decision_prompt had NO length budget anywhere; send_telegram_direct RAISES on a non-2xx; the sweep caught that into a bare `failed += 1`; and the error string went only to the systemd journal, whose retention this repo has itself measured at ~30 minutes. So the channel failed permanently while reporting every health field good. THE PARTITION, over the COMPLETE population of 33 decision requests in docs/claude/work/objects/*.yaml cross-checked against the live marker file (20 markers): 0 of 5 over-cap requests had EVER been delivered, against 20 of 20 delivered markers all UNDER the cap. Unanswered AND over cap = 4 -- EXACTLY the receipt's candidates 4 / failed 4 on 46 of 47 recoverable runs. POSITIVE CONTROL, in situ on the receipt: the largest prompt ever delivered is 3815 chars, and the 47th run reads candidates 5 / failed 4 / prompted_choice 1 -- a 3815-char newcomer went out cleanly on the very same run the four over-cap ones failed. THE FOUR UNDELIVERED: DEC-20260917-SCALP-MARGIN-BOUND-SIZING (5463), DEC-20260913-FOUR-LEG-DISPOSITION (4738), DEC-20260917-NETTING-ATTRIBUTION-EVIDENCE-IS-DROPPABLE (4569), DEC-20260912-LOUD-FLAG-TRIAGE (4184). [!] THE SECOND FINDING IS THE MORE GENERAL ONE AND IS WHY THIS ROW EXISTS RATHER THAN A CLOSED BACKLOG LINE: the sweep wrote a durable receipt on EVERY run and NOTHING READ IT. Detection was never the missing half -- the receipt had the numbers all along. WHAT SHIPPED (PR TBD, Tier-2, landing: hold): the render is bounded as a POST-CONDITION for every input, dropping by load-bearingness (context first, then option implications, the question LAST) and saying so in the body while naming the object YAML; `failure_kinds` + a redacted `failure_detail` name WHY per request; and `sweep_outcome` is registered with collapsed-state-guard as telegram_decisions.sweep_outcome with a real reader in src/runtime/decision_channel_alert.py that pages through outcomes.jsonl. [!] MERGED IS NOT DEPLOYED, DEPLOYED IS NOT DELIVERED, AND DELIVERED IS NOT ANSWERED. It needs a Tier-2 merge, an ict-telegram-bot.service restart, and then a human."}
