ed justification is per-file and was never checked per-file"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "(1) `stale_decisions` distinguishes a cell that CAN be re-swept from one that cannot -- e.g. a `remedy` field per row (`resweep` / `neighbourhood_only` / `not_regradeable`), so a reviewer is never handed an alarm whose implied action is impossible. Three states, not a boolean: 'not yet re-swept', 're-swept', and 'cannot be re-swept' are different, and collapsing the third into the first is what produces the walk-past. (2) The neighbourhood evidence that DOES exist is reachable from the cell -- the trail_geometry cells for htf_pullback_trend_2h and tlt_pullback_1h reference their 2026-08-13 live-parity neighbour rows, so a reader is not left believing nothing has been measured. (3) Either a way to grade a shipped trail_mult is built (the natural one: compare the shipped value against its neighbours as the cell grid already does, and say so explicitly) or the matrix records that trail_geometry decisions are permanently ungradeable post-hoc and the stale flag is scoped accordingly.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-STALE-DECISION-LIST-HOLDS-CELLS-NO-RESWEEP-CAN-CLEAR", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-STALE-DECISION-LIST-HOLDS-CELLS-NO-RESWEEP-CAN-CLEAR", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-STALE-DECISION-LIST-HOLDS-CELLS-NO-RESWEEP-CAN-CLEAR'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] 4 of the 5 remaining stale live DECISIONS are trail_geometry cells that no re-sweep can ever clear -- the list asks for a remedy that does not exist for them"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "(1) A lever-OFF sweep runs over these nine (leg, lever) pairs at live parity (--tp-cap-pct 0.099, --without-declared-lever <lever>) and the rows land in the corpus. (2) Each of the nine cells' `ref` records the OFF-arm result -- the d_net_r_OOS, the verdict, and base_trades_OOS -- so a reader can see whether the shipped lever earns its place, the same way the 22 already-swept pairs do. (3) Any cell whose OFF arm shows the shipped lever is WORSE than its absence is raised to the operator as a Tier-3 disposition question; the row is NOT closed by silently re-grading a live cell. (4) A cell whose OFF arm returns `insufficient_base` is recorded as such -- 'we could not grade it' is a third state and must not read as 'the lever is fine'.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-NINE-SHIPPED-LEVERS-NEVER-GRADED-AGAINST-THEIR-OWN-ABSENCE", "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-NINE-SHIPPED-LEVERS-NEVER-GRADED-AGAINST-THEIR-OWN-ABSENCE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-NINE-SHIPPED-LEVERS-NEVER-GRADED-AGAINST-THEIR-OWN-ABSENCE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] 6 SHIPPED levers have no lever-OFF row — never graded against their own absence (was filed as 9; 2 were never gradeable and 1 was a stale matrix cell)"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "(1) `tp_geometry` is DEFINED in the matrix's `legend` alongside the status values, including what an ABSENT value means — and absence must be given an explicit name (e.g. `unrecorded`) rather than left as null, so 'we did not look' is sayable. (2) Cells whose evidence post-dates the 2026-08-10 cutover AND whose ref names a live-parity run are stamped `live_parity`; cells whose ref predates it are stamped `no_take_profit`. Where the ref does not establish either, the cell is stamped `unrecorded` — NOT guessed from the date alone, since a date is a proxy and this row exists because a proxy was trusted. (3) A guard asserts that every cell carries one of the defined values, so a new cell cannot be added silent. It must ship with a planted-omission self-test. (4) The roll-up reports geometry coverage as a fraction the way `rCoverage`/`pnlCoverage` do, so a reader sees the denominator instead of inferring completeness from the marked cells.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-TP-GEOMETRY-RECORDED-ON-2-PERCENT-OF-CELLS-SO-ABSENCE-CANNOT-MEAN-ANYTHING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-TP-GEOMETRY-RECORDED-ON-2-PERCENT-OF-CELLS-SO-ABSENCE-CANNOT-MEAN-ANYTHING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-TP-GEOMETRY-RECORDED-ON-2-PERCENT-OF-CELLS-SO-ABSENCE-CANNOT-MEAN-ANYTHING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] tp_geometry is set on 10 of 416 coverage cells (2.4%) and documented in neither _doc nor legend — the field that exists to stop one specific wrong inference cannot stop it"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "1. [MET 2026-08-16, verified live 2026-08-23 — /api/diag/ib_open_orders returned read_state='orders_read' with 4 resting ib_paper legs and read_state='could_not_look' with count=null for ib_live, the three-state contract behaving as designed] ADD AN IB OPEN-ORDERS READ SURFACE FIRST (Tier-1, no order path). Without it none of the fixes below can be verified and the next occurrence is equally invisible. Safe to ship alone.\n2. Make protection TRADE-attributable, not symbol-attributable: persist the placed OCA group + leg ids onto the trade row (the columns already exist for Bybit) and have place_protective cancel only the CALLING trade's own legs.\n3. [MET 2026-08-16 — protection_coverage returns stop_qty and target_qty SEPARATELY beside the back-compat covered_qty, classifying each leg through _protective_leg_side with the STOP family tested FIRST so a 'STP LMT' cannot manufacture target coverage; has_protective_orders keeps the combined test deliberately, that being its own question, and its docstring now forbids naked-detection use] Make has_protective_orders return COVERED QUANTITY (or None when unconfirmable) instead of a boolean and compare to the exchange position size - the PR #8000 Bybit shape. Skip rather than guess when coverage is ungradeable.\n4. Reconcile the detection/cancellation scope asymmetry explicitly: both read reqAllOpenOrders, or document the difference as intentional WITH the restart-stacking consequence stated.\n5. [RESOLVED 2026-08-23, was HELD — the ope …[truncated]", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-IB-PROTECTION-BOOLEAN-NOT-QUANTITY", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-IB-PROTECTION-BOOLEAN-NOT-QUANTITY", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-IB-PROTECTION-BOOLEAN-NOT-QUANTITY'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Why the MGC take-profit never fired: IB protective-leg DETECTION is account-wide+boolean while CANCELLATION is session-scoped+symbol-wide - no trade owns its bracket, and nothing can verify one exists"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "Either (a) make the renderer accept the string form the skill documents (coerce str -> {'summary': s}), or (b) fix the skill prose to state the dict/list shapes and point at the template. EITHER WAY, --strict must fail with a NAMED key and expected type instead of an AttributeError - a validator whose failure mode is a stack trace teaches nothing. Add a fixture test that renders the exact payload shape the skill's prose describes.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-SYSTEM-REPORT-SKILL-SHAPES-CONTRADICT-RENDERER", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-SYSTEM-REPORT-SKILL-SHAPES-CONTRADICT-RENDERER", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-SYSTEM-REPORT-SKILL-SHAPES-CONTRADICT-RENDERER'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The /system-review SKILL documents review_coverage blocks as STRINGS; render_system_report.py --strict requires DICTS and dies on AttributeError"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "1. Measure the probe-timeout rate over a WARM window of at least 30 minutes (n>1 process, not a single post-restart burst) -- the honest denominator is timeouts per connect(), not timeouts per minute.\n2. Establish whether attempt 1 EVER succeeds on this relay; if it effectively never does, the 5s first attempt is pure latency and IB_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S should be retuned (Tier-2 env flip) or the first attempt shortened, rather than left as a tax paid on every call.\n3. Decide the log level deliberately: a condition firing on every connect is either normal (and should not be logged per-occurrence at all) or abnormal (and must not sit at INFO). It is currently logged as if it were rare, which is what let it run unnoticed.\n4. Do NOT 'fix' this by widening the retry -- that is what hid it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-IB-LIVENESS-PROBE-TIMES-OUT-EVERY-CONNECT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-IB-LIVENESS-PROBE-TIMES-OUT-EVERY-CONNECT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-IB-LIVENESS-PROBE-TIMES-OUT-EVERY-CONNECT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] IBClient liveness probe attempt 1/2 times out on essentially EVERY connect -- 14 times in 89s -- burning ~5s of dead wait per IB call; the retry saves it, so nothing alarms"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "`legalize_qty` distinguishes at least three states for the ceiling and no consumer sees only one: (a) a resolved maximum, (b) the venue genuinely publishes none, (c) **we could not look** (lookup raised / timed out / returned nothing). On (c) the order path must REFUSE rather than send unclamped - the same fail-safe posture the reconcilers take on an unreadable broker read ('never attribute on an unconfirmed read'). Registering the contract with `collapsed-state-guard` is how it stops regressing. A cheap complement, not a substitute: give `config/instruments.yaml` a maxOrderQty so the offline profile can answer at all - today it structurally cannot, which is why (c) is the common case and not the rare one. Done-condition: a forced lookup failure produces a refusal with a typed reason, and NOT an exchange_rejected row.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260814-VENUE-MAX-NONE-CANNOT-SAY-WE-COULD-NOT-LOOK", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260814-VENUE-MAX-NONE-CANNOT-SAY-WE-COULD-NOT-LOOK", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260814-VENUE-MAX-NONE-CANNOT-SAY-WE-COULD-NOT-LOOK'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] legalize_qty's venue_max=None collapses 'the venue published no maximum' with 'we could not resolve one' - so the BL-20260810 clamp silently no-ops and the oversized order is still sent"}
