{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "1. SHIPPED: close() cancels its own order on the not-confirmed path and declares the outcome three ways -- cancelled / already_filled (a fill raced the cancel; nothing rests and the position may now be FLAT) / cancel_failed (an order STILL RESTS). Never collapsed to a boolean.\n2. SHIPPED: the symbol-wide cancel returns {seen, cancelled, failed, account_wide_seen} and WARNs when the account holds more legs than this session can see. account_wide_seen is None when that read failed -- not zero.\n3. NOT DONE, deliberately: the symbol-wide READ is not widened to reqAllOpenOrders. Cancelling is symbol-wide and one IB symbol's legs span several trades, so widening the read before the cancel is TRADE-scoped would let one partial close strip every sibling's protection -- a bigger blast radius than this bug. That is criterion 2/4 of BL-20260814-IB-PROTECTION-BOOLEAN-NOT-QUANTITY.\n4. OPEN: no wire exists to cancel ONE IB order. The allowlist has cancel-stale-tpsl-legs (Bybit only). Needed for the existing stranded order 6, and blocked on an unverified question -- IB documents cancellation as own-client-only unless the client holds the gateway MASTER client id, and the placing ops session has exited with a PID-derived id. reqGlobalCancel would work but cancels everything including the stop.\n5. LIVE VERIFICATION: after deploy, a failed close must leave ZERO abandoned orders on /api/diag/ib_open_orders. Until that read exists this is untested against a real gateway.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260816-IB-CLOSE-ABANDONS-ITS-OWN-ORDER", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260816-IB-CLOSE-ABANDONS-ITS-OWN-ORDER", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260816-IB-CLOSE-ABANDONS-ITS-OWN-ORDER'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] IBClient.close ABANDONS the market order it just placed when the flatten is not confirmed flat -- so a failed close leaves MORE resting sell orders than it started with, and every retry adds one"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "/api/diag/log_file?name=tick_cost_soak (or an equivalent durable surface) returns rows spanning at least TWO distinct process_started_utc values, and its summary max/mean are computed over the whole file rather than the returned page -- verified by a live read taken AFTER a trader restart, with the summary's tick count exceeding the in-memory ticks_measured of the then-current process. Until that read exists the row stays open; a merged writer is not sufficient, for the same reason #9614 shipped an account_id column that no code path could populate and passed its tests.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260816-TICK-COST-HAS-NO-DURABLE-HALF-SO-A-BUSY-MERGE-DAY-CANNOT-BE-MEASURED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260816-TICK-COST-HAS-NO-DURABLE-HALF-SO-A-BUSY-MERGE-DAY-CANNOT-BE-MEASURED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260816-TICK-COST-HAS-NO-DURABLE-HALF-SO-A-BUSY-MERGE-DAY-CANNOT-BE-MEASURED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] /api/diag/tick_cost counters are per-PROCESS with no durable sibling, so on a day with frequent merges every read is small-n and the tick regression cannot be measured at a useful sample size"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "The operator has recorded a decision on EACH default (change it, or keep it with a dated 'keep' rationale), and that decision lives somewhere a review cadence reads -- this row closed, or the value changed in m20_fleet_exit_sweep.py with the memo section 4 updated to match. A merged code change alone does NOT close it: the other half is that already-recorded sweep numbers get re-interpreted or explicitly marked as produced under the old default, which is the part that silently rots otherwise.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260816-TWO-SWEEP-DEFAULTS-ARE-TIER3-AND-LIVE-ONLY-IN-A-DATED-MEMO", "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260816-TWO-SWEEP-DEFAULTS-ARE-TIER3-AND-LIVE-ONLY-IN-A-DATED-MEMO", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260816-TWO-SWEEP-DEFAULTS-ARE-TIER3-AND-LIVE-ONLY-IN-A-DATED-MEMO'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] m20_fleet_exit_sweep's --tp-cap-pct and --split-target-oos defaults are both Tier-3 proposals recorded ONLY in a dated operator memo, which no review cadence drains"}
