{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "OBSERVABLE: two DIFFERENT client objects that occupy the same address at different times must not share a cache entry. Demonstrate with a test that builds a client, caches a frame, drops it, builds a second client that CPython allocates at the same id, and asserts the second gets a MISS — the test must be shown to FAIL against the current id()-based key, or it proves nothing.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260817-CANDLE-CACHE-KEYS-ON-ID-CLIENT-WHICH-CPYTHON-RECYCLES", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260817-CANDLE-CACHE-KEYS-ON-ID-CLIENT-WHICH-CPYTHON-RECYCLES", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260817-CANDLE-CACHE-KEYS-ON-ID-CLIENT-WHICH-CPYTHON-RECYCLES'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] market_data._candle_cache_key keys on id(client), which CPython recycles the instant an object is freed — so the key cannot do the one thing its own comment says it exists for"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "OBSERVABLE: a fold in which the lever never fires must NOT be counted as a win. Either (a) `wf_wins`/`wf_summary` count only folds with a non-zero delta and report the inert count separately, or (b) a fold with `d_net_r == 0.0 and d_max_dd == 0.0` gets a distinct third state (not `ok: True`), registered with collapsed-state-guard so producer and consumer are both checked. PLUS a planted control: a cell whose folds are all inert must not come back `6/6`, demonstrated by RUNNING it — a quiet pass proves nothing. AND the fold window must state its coverage against the OOS window, so a delta originating outside every fold cannot read as walk-forward-confirmed.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260817-FLEET-SWEEP-WF-COUNTS-INERT-FOLDS-AS-WINS", "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260817-FLEET-SWEEP-WF-COUNTS-INERT-FOLDS-AS-WINS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260817-FLEET-SWEEP-WF-COUNTS-INERT-FOLDS-AS-WINS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] m20_fleet_exit_sweep's walk-forward reports `wf_summary: 6/6` on six folds where the lever changed NOTHING — and the folds do not cover the years the OOS delta comes from"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "The row closes when ALL of these hold:\n1. A DIRECT answer for FUT, sourced from IBKR documentation quoted verbatim with a URL, or from a paired live experiment with both arms recorded, or both.\n2. The answer explicitly states whether it covers STK as well, or says it does not.\n3. `BL-20260816-IB-PROTECTIVE-STOPS-NEVER-SET-OUTSIDERTH` is updated with the finding and moved to either a proposed Tier-3 change (if stops ARE inert) or a documented close (if they are not). A close needs the rationale written down, or the next session re-opens it.\n4. EITHER WAY, `protection_coverage` is assessed against the answer: today it reports RESTING quantity and says nothing about trigger eligibility. If eligibility turns out to be a real axis, that is a collapsed state in the coverage verdict and belongs in the collapsed-state registry.\n5. If neither line produces an answer, say so plainly and record WHICH line failed and why. 'Could not establish' is an acceptable outcome; a confident guess is not.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "RS-20260817-DOES-OUTSIDERTH-FALSE-MAKE-A-FUTURES-STOP-INERT", "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#RS-20260817-DOES-OUTSIDERTH-FALSE-MAKE-A-FUTURES-STOP-INERT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='RS-20260817-DOES-OUTSIDERTH-FALSE-MAKE-A-FUTURES-STOP-INERT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] RESEARCH: does outsideRth=False make a GTC futures STOP ineligible to TRIGGER outside RTH? Answer this before anyone changes protective-order geometry"}
