{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "Every prop fill row carries an explicit, never-collapsed pnl BASIS — at minimum `gross` / `net_of_commission` / `unknown` (we could not determine it — never silently folded into either) — and the value is derived, not assumed: `(exit - entry) x qty` reproduces gross from the row's own fields, so `stored_pnl - gross` IS the commission and the basis follows from whether that residual is ~0 or ~the venue's bps. Registered with collapsed-state-guard, and READ by at least one consumer (a stamp with no reader is the exact defect provenance-consumer-guard exists to catch). Any aggregate over prop rows must then state its basis or refuse to mix. NO writeback to the existing rows — they are not wrong, they are unlabelled. SEPARATELY: confirm with the operator when and why the reported basis changed around 2026-08-19, since that boundary is currently recorded nowhere and silently splits the series in two.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260823-PROP-JOURNAL-PNL-DISAGREES-WITH-VENUE-ON-RECENT-ROWS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260823-PROP-JOURNAL-PNL-DISAGREES-WITH-VENUE-ON-RECENT-ROWS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260823-PROP-JOURNAL-PNL-DISAGREES-WITH-VENUE-ON-RECENT-ROWS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The prop PnL series MIXES gross and net-of-commission rows with nothing marking which — CONFIRMED to the cent against the venue's own commission field"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "The rule is stated where a session will actually hit it — a line in `docs/CLAUDE-RULES-CANONICAL.md` under the verification rules: a backgrounded or piped command's reported exit code is the LAST element of the pipeline, so redirect (`> file 2>&1`) and echo the real `$?` into the file rather than piping, and never pre-filter a long-running run's output at capture time. Resolution requires the rule to be written down, not merely remembered — this row exists because remembering it twice did not work.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260823-BACKGROUND-TASK-RC-IS-THE-PIPELINE-NOT-THE-COMMAND", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260823-BACKGROUND-TASK-RC-IS-THE-PIPELINE-NOT-THE-COMMAND", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260823-BACKGROUND-TASK-RC-IS-THE-PIPELINE-NOT-THE-COMMAND'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A background task's completion notification reports the PIPELINE's exit code, so `pytest … | tail` completes as 'exit code 0' while 12 tests are failing"}
