{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "1. The operating rule, which is the cheap and durable half: when polling CI, read `actions_get method=get_workflow_run` and treat `updated_at` as the freshness signal. Do NOT conclude `in_progress` from `get_check_runs` or `list_workflow_jobs` alone, and NEVER cancel or re-dispatch on that basis. Land it wherever the merge/CI practice is written down so it is reachable by a session that has not read this row.\n2. Establish whether the lag is the hosted GitHub MCP's caching or GitHub's own API. Not attempted here — the direct REST API is unreachable from this sandbox (it 403s, per CLAUDE.md), so the two cannot be compared from a web session. A CLI session could settle it in one call.\n3. If it is MCP-side caching it is not fixable from this repo, and the rule in (1) is the whole remedy — which is fine, and is why (1) does not depend on (2).", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260825-GITHUB-CHECK-RUN-READS-LAG-AND-READ-AS-STILL-RUNNING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260825-GITHUB-CHECK-RUN-READS-LAG-AND-READ-AS-STILL-RUNNING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260825-GITHUB-CHECK-RUN-READS-LAG-AND-READ-AS-STILL-RUNNING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] mcp__github check-run and job reads lag by tens of minutes on this repo, so a COMPLETED check reads as `in_progress` — and a session waiting on CI concludes the job is hung"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "1. A fetch failure must not abort the deploy silently. Either retry the fetch once (a ref-lock race is resolved by the next attempt, as this occurrence demonstrates), or let the script CONTINUE to the restart-decision gate — the gate reads deployed_sha.txt against the worktree and does not need the fetch to have succeeded to notice that the running processes are stale.\n2. A FAILED deploy must be loud. `ict-git-sync.service` entering `failed` is currently visible only to someone who reads /api/diag/services or the unit journal; nothing alerts. Note this is the same shape as the over-cover detector before 2026-08-25 — correctly detected, reaching no surface a human reads.\n3. Do NOT 'fix' this by making the fetch non-fatal without also reaching the gate: swallowing the error and proceeding to a hard-reset against a stale ref would be worse than the abort.\n4. Establish whether `git fetch --prune` or a ref-lock retry is the cleaner remedy. Not investigated here.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260825-GIT-FETCH-REF-LOCK-RACE-ABORTS-THE-DEPLOY-UPSTREAM-OF-ITS-OWN-STALE-CODE-GATE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260825-GIT-FETCH-REF-LOCK-RACE-ABORTS-THE-DEPLOY-UPSTREAM-OF-ITS-OWN-STALE-CODE-GATE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260825-GIT-FETCH-REF-LOCK-RACE-ABORTS-THE-DEPLOY-UPSTREAM-OF-ITS-OWN-STALE-CODE-GATE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A concurrent-fetch ref-lock race makes `git fetch` exit non-zero, which aborts deploy_pull_restart.sh BEFORE its restart-decision gate — so the worktree advances and the live processes keep