{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "Establish WHICH term folded dry: read PROP/effective_dry inputs on the RUNNING process (a get-env read of the account mode against /proc/<MainPID>/environ plus the process's loaded accounts.yaml), not the repo copy. Then EITHER the running config is stale, in which case the fix is the deploy/restart path and the finding is that ict-git-sync left a Tier-3-approved routing unapplied for 5+ days; OR a third dry-fold term exists, in which case name it and cover it with a test. Closed when a tlt_pullback_1h signal on alpaca_live is journalled with a status other than 'rejected', or when the operator records a decision that the account stays dry.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260906-ALPACA-LIVE-FOLDS-DRY-RUN-WHILE-ACCOUNTS-YAML-AND-THE-STRATEGY-BOTH-DECLARE-LIVE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260906-ALPACA-LIVE-FOLDS-DRY-RUN-WHILE-ACCOUNTS-YAML-AND-THE-STRATEGY-BOTH-DECLARE-LIVE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260906-ALPACA-LIVE-FOLDS-DRY-RUN-WHILE-ACCOUNTS-YAML-AND-THE-STRATEGY-BOTH-DECLARE-LIVE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] alpaca_live's routed real-money leg cannot place an order: both declared gates read live, yet every signal since the 2026-08-31 routing is journalled 'dry_run_no_order_placed'"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "rCoverage either (a) reports the share of rows with a VERIFIED risk basis, so the published number moves with rProvenance rather than contradicting it, or (b) is renamed/rescoped to what it actually measures AND an honest coverage figure is published beside it. Either way it must be able to express 'we did not look' — a zero-trade window must not read 0.0 as if that were a measurement, matching pnlCoverage's None. VERIFY BY RE-READING /api/bot/performance on at least two windows and showing rCoverage and rProvenance now agree; a passing unit test is NOT this observation. Consider registering the field with collapsed-state-guard.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260906-RCOVERAGE-REPORTS-1-0-WHILE-90-PERCENT-OF-ROWS-ARE-UNVERIFIED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260906-RCOVERAGE-REPORTS-1-0-WHILE-90-PERCENT-OF-ROWS-ARE-UNVERIFIED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260906-RCOVERAGE-REPORTS-1-0-WHILE-90-PERCENT-OF-ROWS-ARE-UNVERIFIED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] rCoverage publishes 1.0 while its own rProvenance block on the same payload reads 381 of 424 unverified (89.9%)"}
