{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A writer for each guarded register that CANNOT produce a row the guard rejects, modelled on backlog_append.py: (a) docs/claude/OPEN-ITEMS.json - and it must fix the round-trip problem or own the splice itself, so no caller ever hand-edits it again; (b) docs/claude/work/MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json; (c) .github/pr-landing/<slug>.json, which can DERIVE the slug from the branch rather than having the author retype it. VERIFY BY PLANTING: for each writer, attempt a row the corresponding guard rejects and show the writer REFUSES it at write time - a passing guard on a well-formed row proves nothing, since that is the case that already works. !! DO NOT WEAKEN ANY GUARD. The guards are the only reason these classes are visible at all; the fix is upstream of them. !! AND DO NOT BUILD A SCAFFOLD THAT ONLY EMITS A TEMPLATE - a template the author edits by hand reintroduces exactly the omissions measured above. The writer must validate what it is about to write. SEPARATELY AND SMALLER: scripts/ops/manager_lease.py has --commit but its help says 'never pushes', while the lease's own canonical rule is 'a claim you did not PUSH protects nothing - another session reads origin, not your working tree'. A tool that stops one step short of its own doc's requirement is a trap; either it pushes, or it says loudly that the lease is not yet protecting anything.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260906-EVERY-REGISTER-WRITE-IS-A-GUESS-THEN-A-CI-ROUND-TRIP", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260906-EVERY-REGISTER-WRITE-IS-A-GUESS-THEN-A-CI-ROUND-TRIP", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260906-EVERY-REGISTER-WRITE-IS-A-GUESS-THEN-A-CI-ROUND-TRIP'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The operating-layer registers are guarded but not scaffolded, so every write is discovered wrong by CI ~2 minutes later"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "An artifact that SPECIFIES WORK cannot be created without a register row pointing at it, AND un-actioned specs are visible at session start. Candidates, not a design: (a) a CI check failing a PR that adds docs/research/*SESSION-PROMPT*.md / *-PROPOSAL-*.md / *-DESIGN.md with no matching work object referencing its path; (b) a rendered SESSION-BRIEF section listing specs with no owning object - the surface that demonstrably reaches a session before it acts; (c) a sweep grepping for artifacts whose own text asks for a follow-up ('paste this as', 'next session should', 'not yet built') and filing any with no carrier. VERIFY BY PLANTING a spec with no carrier and showing the mechanism catches it, AND by running it over the existing tree and REPORTING HOW MANY UN-CARRIED SPECS ALREADY EXIST - that count is the finding and is currently UNMEASURED (now owned by WO-20260906-COUNT-THE-UN-CARRIED-SPECS, operator-chosen 2026-09-06). !! A mechanism covering only NEW artifacts leaves the existing pile invisible; say which half you built. !! The 14-day gap was NOT someone forgetting - the artifact was well-written and correctly filed. There was no path from 'filed' to 'planned'. A fix relying on sessions filing better does not address the cause.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260906-A-RESEARCH-ARTIFACT-THAT-SPECIFIES-WORK-IS-NOT-REGISTERED-AS-WORK", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260906-A-RESEARCH-ARTIFACT-THAT-SPECIFIES-WORK-IS-NOT-REGISTERED-AS-WORK", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260906-A-RESEARCH-ARTIFACT-THAT-SPECIFIES-WORK-IS-NOT-REGISTERED-AS-WORK'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A finished session prompt sat undispatched 14 days because docs/research/ is not a work register - and the same thesis was re-derived seven times"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A session measuring a condition its own cycle has been remediating states WHICH SHA its control was graded at, and why that sha is uncontaminated. Cheap, mechanical form: grade the negative control in a worktree at the last commit before the current cycle's work began, and record that sha beside the result -- scripts/ops/uncarried_specs.py --self-test --strict-negative is a worked example (it REFUSES to pass unless the known-stranded artifact grades un-carried on a pre-remediation tree). !! DO NOT 'FIX' THIS BY DROPPING THE CONTROL: the contaminated control still passed, so removing it loses the only thing that caught the under-count. !! AND A PROBE WITH NO NEGATIVE CONTROL AT ALL IS WORSE THAN A CONTAMINATED ONE -- it cannot be wrong in a way anyone notices.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260906-A-CONTROL-MEASURED-AFTER-YOUR-OWN-REMEDIATION-CONFIRMS-THE-FIX-INSTEAD-OF-TESTING-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260906-A-CONTROL-MEASURED-AFTER-YOUR-OWN-REMEDIATION-CONFIRMS-THE-FIX-INSTEAD-OF-TESTING-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260906-A-CONTROL-MEASURED-AFTER-YOUR-OWN-REMEDIATION-CONFIRMS-THE-FIX-INSTEAD-OF-TESTING-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A negative control graded at HEAD was carried by work objects this week's own program created that same day — the control confirmed the remediation instead of testing the condition"}
