{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "BOTH, and they are different facts — say which you cleared. (1) PREVENTION: a spawn cannot omit the repo — either create_session is wrapped so source_url is always supplied, or a spawn with no explicit source_url is REFUSED. Verified by a NEW session appearing in list_sessions carrying the correct repo without its prompt having said anything about repos. (2) DETECTION: a session establishes its own repo from get_session BEFORE substantive work and stops if it is wrong — verified by observing a real session report the check, not by a spawn prompt containing the instruction. NOT SUFFICIENT: another backlog row, another line in a spawn template, or a push probe passing (the probe detects the symptom and names no cause). NOT SUFFICIENT: a quiet week — the class ran at 5/day on 2026-09-08 and 0/day on 2026-09-05, so absence over a short window is not evidence.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-PUSH-DENIED-AND-WRONG-REPO-ARE-ONE-DEFECT-3-OF-3-AND-A-ONE-CALL-PREDICTOR-EXISTS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-PUSH-DENIED-AND-WRONG-REPO-ARE-ONE-DEFECT-3-OF-3-AND-A-ONE-CALL-PREDICTOR-EXISTS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-PUSH-DENIED-AND-WRONG-REPO-ARE-ONE-DEFECT-3-OF-3-AND-A-ONE-CALL-PREDICTOR-EXISTS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] RECURRENCE + UNIFICATION: the 'container cannot push' class and the 'spawned without source_url' class are ONE defect — 3 of 3 push-denied sessions carried a wrong or absent repo, and a session can predict it in ONE get_session call before spending any budget"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A row claiming an active state either CARRIES a dateable observation under ONE agreed key, or is rendered as STALE rather than as fact. Verified by reading SESSIONS.json at a moment when a session is known to have died and finding its row NOT asserting `working` — i.e. observe the decay happening, not the mechanism existing. THREE STATES MUST STAY APART: observed-active / observed-inactive / NOT-OBSERVED-SINCE-<t>; collapsing the third into the first is the present bug. NOT SUFFICIENT: a reconcile pass run by hand (three have been run and the rows went false again within the hour); the state_observed_at field merely EXISTING (it exists now, on 6 of 164 rows); or a green guard — check_manager_scope R6 already grades the RECORD of supervision and cannot see a row that is simply old.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-A-WORKING-REGISTRY-ROW-HAS-A-MEASURED-HALF-LIFE-OF-61-MINUTES-SO-ANY-DECAY-RULE-SLOWER-THAN-THAT-IS-WRONG-ABOUT-HALF-ITS-ROWS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-A-WORKING-REGISTRY-ROW-HAS-A-MEASURED-HALF-LIFE-OF-61-MINUTES-SO-ANY-DECAY-RULE-SLOWER-THAN-THAT-IS-WRONG-ABOUT-HALF-ITS-ROWS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-A-WORKING-REGISTRY-ROW-HAS-A-MEASURED-HALF-LIFE-OF-61-MINUTES-SO-ANY-DECAY-RULE-SLOWER-THAN-THAT-IS-WRONG-ABOUT-HALF-ITS-ROWS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] SESSIONS.json rows go false BY TIME PASSING, and the decay curve is now measured: median truth-lifetime 61.3 min, 47.9% dead within the hour — the number the existing 'no close writer' rows name the defect without supplying"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A guard pair whose satisfying sets are disjoint is detected BEFORE it reds main. Verified by the detector firing on a DELIBERATELY CONSTRUCTED conflicting pair that is not one of the two known instances — a detector validated only against the cases it was written from proves nothing. It must cover BOTH sub-shapes or say explicitly which one it does not cover: a path-only detector that stays silent on a content conflict is the unprovenanced-diagnostic shape (a clean negative that checked one of two conditions). NOT SUFFICIENT: fixing the two live instances (MI-191 is doing that; it removes two points, not the class); a green guard suite (both instances were green ALONE); or an enumeration whose candidates are un-adjudicated — 19 candidates with 1 verified is not a detector, it is a list.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-NO-GUARD-DECLARES-ITS-SATISFYING-SET-SO-A-DEADLOCKED-PAIR-CAN-ONLY-BE-FOUND-BY-HITTING-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-NO-GUARD-DECLARES-ITS-SATISFYING-SET-SO-A-DEADLOCKED-PAIR-CAN-ONLY-BE-FOUND-BY-HITTING-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-NO-GUARD-DECLARES-ITS-SATISFYING-SET-SO-A-DEADLOCKED-PAIR-CAN-ONLY-BE-FOUND-BY-HITTING-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Individually-correct guards deadlock in two distinct sub-shapes (path polarity, content polarity) and neither is enumerable today, because a guard declares what it CHECKS and never which actor must write which path or content"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 45, "clears_when": "Either (a) add `actions: read` to due-list.yml's permissions block and OBSERVE a scheduled run whose committed DUE.json still shows `red_crons: read` — the observation is the point, since adding the scope cannot be distinguished from the public-repo path by reading the file; or (b) establish by reading a real run's log that `contents` already suffices, and record THAT, so a future session does not re-derive the question. NOT sufficient: the source continuing to read while the repo stays public — that is the condition being questioned, not evidence against it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-DUE-LIST-RED-CRONS-DEPENDS-ON-THE-REPO-BEING-PUBLIC-NOT-ON-A-DECLARED-PERMISSION", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-DUE-LIST-RED-CRONS-DEPENDS-ON-THE-REPO-BEING-PUBLIC-NOT-ON-A-DECLARED-PERMISSION", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-DUE-LIST-RED-CRONS-DEPENDS-ON-THE-REPO-BEING-PUBLIC-NOT-ON-A-DECLARED-PERMISSION'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] due-list.yml grants no `actions: read`, so its red-crons source works only because the repo is public"}
