{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, and they are different facts — say which you closed. (1) THE BLIND SPOT: over-cover is detectable when a position carries BOTH a Full-mode position-level stop AND resting Partial legs. That needs the full_position_stop branch to stop returning before it has looked, or a separate leg-count read; note it costs a get_open_orders call the branch currently avoids, so it is a real trade-off and not a free fix. Proven by an observed over-cover page on a mixed-mode bracket, never by a test. (2) THE RE-ARM: the adopt path's naked re-arm consults existing broker coverage before placing, or cancels the closing row's tracked legs. ⚠️ DO NOT RESOLVE (2) BY CANCELLING LEGS ON THE LIVE POSITION AS A ONE-OFF — BL-20260820-OVERCOVER-REMEDIATION-CANCELLED-THE-JOURNAL-MATCHING-LEG is what happened the last time that was attempted. The current 200% instance is expected to clear when the root cause lands and this position closes normally; if it clears that way, that is NOT evidence either half is fixed.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-A-FULL-MODE-NAKED-REARM-OVER-PARTIAL-LEGS-DOUBLES-THE-COVER-AND-THE-OVER-COVER-PAGE-IS-BLIND-TO-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-A-FULL-MODE-NAKED-REARM-OVER-PARTIAL-LEGS-DOUBLES-THE-COVER-AND-THE-OVER-COVER-PAGE-IS-BLIND-TO-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-A-FULL-MODE-NAKED-REARM-OVER-PARTIAL-LEGS-DOUBLES-THE-COVER-AND-THE-OVER-COVER-PAGE-IS-BLIND-TO-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The adopt path's naked re-arm places a Full-mode bracket over still-resting Partial legs, doubling the cover — and the over-cover trip is structurally blind to it because a Full-mode stop makes the reader return before it ever lists the legs"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "The adopt path refuses to write a strategy_name it cannot support. Concretely: a quantity check against the claimed strategy's own recent size history on that symbol — the cheapest available discriminator, and one that would have refused BOTH wrong attributions here — and on failure the row is left a BARE orphan (recovered_strategy empty, which 6 of 13 correctly already are) rather than attributed to a guess. A bare orphan is the honest state; a wrong attribution is worse than none because it reads as known and is acted on. PROVEN BY: an observed adopt whose re-attach DECLINED on a quantity mismatch and left the row bare, read from the live journal — not by a unit test, which cannot reproduce the venue state that produces a candidate package. ALSO REQUIRED: the two existing OUTSIDE rows (5448, 5453) are dispositioned — either corrected with the reason recorded, or explicitly left with a note that their strategy_name is not trustworthy, so a later aggregate does not silently consume them. NOT SUFFICIENT: fixing the rows[0] root cause (BL-20260908-BYBIT-POSITION-PROTECTION-GRADES-A-SYMBOL-OFF-ROWS0-SO-A-HEDGE-BOOK-READS-FLAT-AND-A-LIVE-POSITION-IS-CLOSED). That reduces how OFTEN adopts happen and does not make the attribution correct when one does; the two defects are independent and 5453's parent chain does not involve a netting false close at all.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-THE-ORPHAN-ADOPT-REATTACH-WRITES-A-STRATEGY-NAME-IT-CANNOT-SUPPORT-AND-THAT-STRATEGY-THEN-ACTS-ON-THE-ROW", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-THE-ORPHAN-ADOPT-REATTACH-WRITES-A-STRATEGY-NAME-IT-CANNOT-SUPPORT-AND-THAT-STRATEGY-THEN-ACTS-ON-THE-ROW", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-THE-ORPHAN-ADOPT-REATTACH-WRITES-A-STRATEGY-NAME-IT-CANNOT-SUPPORT-AND-THAT-STRATEGY-THEN-ACTS-ON-THE-ROW'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The reverse reconciler's orphan re-attach can name a strategy that did not open the position — it wrote +$612.71 of trend_donchian_eth's PnL onto pairs_sol_eth_b, and the pairs executor then flattened the position 14s later"}
