{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "MEASURED 2026-09-08 on a LIVE instance: PR #11347 (branch `mi-168-post-merge-record`) declares tier 1 / landing self, writes .github/pr-automerge-requests/mi-168-post-merge-record.txt, passes `pr-landing: OK - state=declared_self_land`, is GREEN on all 5 checks and `mergeable_state: clean` - and does not merge, because .github/workflows/claude-pr-automerge.yml is `on: push: branches: [\"claude/**\"]` and the branch is not under `claude/`. The workflow never fires at all. !! THE GUARD STRIPS THE PREFIX BUT NEVER REQUIRES IT. check_pr_landing.py:256 derives the slug as `re.sub(r'^claude/', '', branch).replace('/', '-')` - so a `claude/` prefix is OPTIONAL for slug derivation, and R6 then checks only that the request FILE exists and differs from base. Nothing checks that the branch NAME can reach the workflow. So R6 certifies an arming that is inert by construction. !! IT IS INVISIBLE TO THE GUARD'S OWN SELF-TEST BECAUSE EVERY FIXTURE USES A TRIGGERABLE NAME: check_pr_landing.py:516 creates `claude/demo` and the R6 case at :621 runs against it, so the one branch shape that breaks is the one shape never tested. A positive control passing is what made this survivable to ship. !! DISTINCT FROM BL-20260903-A-PR-OPENED-BY-THE-RELAY-CAN-ARM-AUTOMERGE-AND-THEN-WAIT-ON-GREEN-FOREVER, AND THE TWO MUST NOT BE MERGED: that row is the ZERO-CHECKS cause (a relay-opened PR starts with no checks because the results commit is pushed by github-actions[bot], and auto-merge waits on a green that nev …[truncated]", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260908-PR-LANDING-ARMS-A-ROUTE-THAT-CANNOT-FIRE-ON-A-NON-CLAUDE-BRANCH", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260908-PR-LANDING-ARMS-A-ROUTE-THAT-CANNOT-FIRE-ON-A-NON-CLAUDE-BRANCH", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260908-PR-LANDING-ARMS-A-ROUTE-THAT-CANNOT-FIRE-ON-A-NON-CLAUDE-BRANCH'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] check_pr_landing R6 certifies `landing: self` on a branch whose NAME cannot trigger claude-pr-automerge (branches: claude/**), so the PR passes its own guard and then never merges — the exact failure the landing system exists to prevent"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A manager pass is observed grading a sub-session's progress WITHOUT using remote-branch presence as the productivity term -- or using it only alongside a stated expectation of first-push latency for that class of task. NOT SUFFICIENT: another backlog row, another line in a wake prompt, or a resolution to be more careful -- this row exists BECAUSE a self-issued instruction to be decisive is what produced the error. What would close it is a cheap POSITIVE probe run before calling a stall: ask the session (create_trigger + fire_trigger, proven to work per BL-20260902-AN-IDLE-CLOUD-SUB-SESSION-IS-RESUMABLE-VIA-A-SESSION-BOUND-ROUTINE-NOT-UNREACHABLE), or read whether its token counters are climbing -- MI-205b's own get_session record showed output_tokens 172,537 and cost_usd 54.03 at the moment it was called unproductive, a directly available counter-signal in a payload the manager had already fetched and did not read.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-MANAGER-GRADED-A-SUBSESSION-UNPRODUCTIVE-FROM-AN-ABSENT-REMOTE-BRANCH-AND-PUBLISHED-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-MANAGER-GRADED-A-SUBSESSION-UNPRODUCTIVE-FROM-AN-ABSENT-REMOTE-BRANCH-AND-PUBLISHED-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-MANAGER-GRADED-A-SUBSESSION-UNPRODUCTIVE-FROM-AN-ABSENT-REMOTE-BRANCH-AND-PUBLISHED-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A manager read 'no branch on the remote' as 'no work produced', called a working session a STALL, and merged that claim to main 28 seconds before the session opened a 29-file PR"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "The repo's own guidance and prompts stop recommending `git reset --hard origin/main` as the sync idiom and use `git checkout main && git pull --ff-only` instead — checked by grepping the instruction surfaces, not by asserting it. ⚠️ NOT SUFFICIENT: another reminder, in any document or wake prompt, that one should check the current branch first. That is precisely what was tried between instance 1 and instance 2 and it failed within the hour; a row closed on a restatement would be closing on the thing already measured not to work. ⚠️ ALSO NOT SUFFICIENT: 'no further instances observed' — the second instance was harmless by luck, so absence of DAMAGE is not absence of the behaviour, and only the harmful case is visible.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-RESET-HARD-ORIGIN-MAIN-ON-A-FEATURE-BRANCH-TWICE-IN-50-MINUTES-AND-THE-WRITTEN-REMINDER-DID-NOT-HOLD", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-RESET-HARD-ORIGIN-MAIN-ON-A-FEATURE-BRANCH-TWICE-IN-50-MINUTES-AND-THE-WRITTEN-REMINDER-DID-NOT-HOLD", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-RESET-HARD-ORIGIN-MAIN-ON-A-FEATURE-BRANCH-TWICE-IN-50-MINUTES-AND-THE-WRITTEN-REMINDER-DID-NOT-HOLD'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] `git reset --hard origin/main` run while standing on a feature branch, twice in ~50 minutes by the same session — the second time AFTER writing the reminder against it on main"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "EITHER (a) a guard that fails a PR whose diff changes the TYPE of an existing value in any docs/claude/work/*.json register row — not just id uniqueness, which check_register_ids already covers — and is observed FAILING on a deliberately-flattened test row, not merely registered; OR (b) `last_observed` is given a declared shape and the 56 null rows are reconciled to it, so a scalar assignment is a type error rather than a silent overwrite. ⚠️ NOT SUFFICIENT: a note in the cadence Routine or in CLAUDE.md telling a manager to be careful — this pass already carried a written warning about registers being append-only and about not taking a side in a merge, and neither covers an in-place field overwrite by the register's own maintainer. ⚠️ ALSO NOT SUFFICIENT: my own value-level assertion, which lives in a throwaway script in one session's context and protects nothing after this turn.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-MANAGER-OVERWROTE-A-STRUCTURED-LAST-OBSERVED-WITH-A-SCALAR-AND-THE-LOSS-PROOF-WAS-BLIND-TO-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-MANAGER-OVERWROTE-A-STRUCTURED-LAST-OBSERVED-WITH-A-SCALAR-AND-THE-LOSS-PROOF-WAS-BLIND-TO-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-MANAGER-OVERWROTE-A-STRUCTURED-LAST-OBSERVED-WITH-A-SCALAR-AND-THE-LOSS-PROOF-WAS-BLIND-TO-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A routine manager reconcile wrote a bare timestamp over SESSIONS.json's structured `last_observed`, destroying nine `manager_verdict` records — and the loss check passed because it tested KEY PRESENCE, not value shape"}
