{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "is_measured (and classify_row) raise TypeError, or return a distinguishable third outcome, when handed a non-mapping — NOT silently UNVERIFIED. Demonstrated by a test asserting BOTH controls: passing a real row with exit_price_source='bybit_closed_pnl' returns True (positive control), and passing the bare string 'measured' does not return False silently. A docstring warning alone does NOT close this — the sibling function already has one and this function is what a caller reaches for first.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-PROVENANCE-IS-MEASURED-RETURNS-FALSE-FOR-EVERY-ROW-WHEN-HANDED-A-BUCKET-STRING-AND-SAYS-NOTHING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-PROVENANCE-IS-MEASURED-RETURNS-FALSE-FOR-EVERY-ROW-WHEN-HANDED-A-BUCKET-STRING-AND-SAYS-NOTHING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-PROVENANCE-IS-MEASURED-RETURNS-FALSE-FOR-EVERY-ROW-WHEN-HANDED-A-BUCKET-STRING-AND-SAYS-NOTHING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] provenance.is_measured(row) accepts Any and silently returns False for EVERY row when passed a bucket string instead of a row — the same total-silent-failure its sibling pnl_is_trustworthy has a docstring warning about"}
