{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "GET /api/diag/log_file accepts an offset (or an explicit head/range) so a caller can page a multi-hundred-KB log to its start, mirroring audit_query's existing limit+offset. Demonstrated on exit_lever_soak by BOTH controls: a paged read reaching the file's FIRST record (positive — the record's ts predates the current 1000-record tail window, which begins 2026-08-31T12:03:15Z), and a request beyond the end returning an empty page rather than silently re-serving the tail (negative — an out-of-range page that returns the last 1000 lines is the collapsed state this row exists to prevent, and would be worse than the cap). Raising _MAX_LIMIT alone does NOT close this: it moves the ceiling without making the file pageable, and a 3,897-record file would need it raised again. Tier-2 because it changes a live-VM web-api route; not built by the filing session, which was measurement-only.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-DIAG-LOG-FILE-IS-TAIL-ONLY-AND-HARD-CAPPED-AT-1000-SO-A-MULTI-HUNDRED-KB-SOAK-CANNOT-BE-READ-OVER-ITS-LIFETIME", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-DIAG-LOG-FILE-IS-TAIL-ONLY-AND-HARD-CAPPED-AT-1000-SO-A-MULTI-HUNDRED-KB-SOAK-CANNOT-BE-READ-OVER-ITS-LIFETIME", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-DIAG-LOG-FILE-IS-TAIL-ONLY-AND-HARD-CAPPED-AT-1000-SO-A-MULTI-HUNDRED-KB-SOAK-CANNOT-BE-READ-OVER-ITS-LIFETIME'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] /api/diag/log_file is tail-only and hard-capped at 1000 lines with NO offset, so a soak log is unreadable beyond its last 1000 records from any session — exit_lever_soak's 1000-record tail covers only ~25.7% of its estimated lifetime"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A CI guard fails when a module under src/ writes a runtime_logs/*_state.json or *_alerts.jsonl path that has no _LOG_FILES entry, unless the writer carries an explicit `# read-surface: none - <reason>` marker. THREE REQUIREMENTS, each from a mistake this repo has already made and none of them optional: (1) THE MARKER MUST BE VERIFIED, NOT PRESENCE-ONLY — it must name something checkable, because new-table-wiring-guard's presence-only `# data-wiring:` marker made the cheapest way to silence a real finding be to name a table that does not exist, and a guard cheaper to lie to than to satisfy is worse than no guard. (2) IT MUST SHIP WITH A SELF-TEST PROVING IT FAILS on a planted writer with no allowlist entry — a guard whose failure path has never executed is a deploy, not a check. (3) IT MUST STATE ITS DENOMINATOR: how many writer sites it scanned, so a guard that silently stops matching (a renamed path helper, a new write idiom) reads as a shrinking population rather than as continued green. ⚠️ NOT SUFFICIENT: adding another name to _LOG_FILES. That is what was done all five times, and it is why there were five. ⚠️ NOT SUFFICIENT: extending the allowlist-vs-CLAUDE.md coherence test, which by construction cannot see an unlisted writer.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-NO-WRITER-SIDE-GUARD-STOPS-A-PAGING-INPUT-SHIPPING-WITHOUT-A-READ-SURFACE-AND-ITS-ONLY-CARRIER-IS-A-RESOLVED-ROW", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-NO-WRITER-SIDE-GUARD-STOPS-A-PAGING-INPUT-SHIPPING-WITHOUT-A-READ-SURFACE-AND-ITS-ONLY-CARRIER-IS-A-RESOLVED-ROW", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-NO-WRITER-SIDE-GUARD-STOPS-A-PAGING-INPUT-SHIPPING-WITHOUT-A-READ-SURFACE-AND-ITS-ONLY-CARRIER-IS-A-RESOLVED-ROW'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Nothing PREVENTS a file that decides whether the operator is paged from shipping with no diag read surface — this is the recurrence half of a FIFTH instance, and its only written carrier is a row already marked `resolved`"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 45, "clears_when": "A prop sizing refusal for a stale/absent balance is OBSERVED reaching the operator — a row in outcomes.jsonl / /api/bot/logs?level=error, or a /api/bot/notifications banner, naming the account and carrying prop_balance's own refusal_message text — read off the live surface, not from a test. ⚠️ A GREEN TEST CLEARS NOTHING: the refusal path is already exercised in tests and the gap is which channel the message reaches. ⚠️ AND A JOURNALED order_packages ROW IS NOT SUFFICIENT — that is precisely the current behaviour and the thing being reported as inadequate. ALTERNATIVELY the operator DECIDES that a silently non-trading prop account needs no alert, which clears this row as a RECORDED decision stating the accepted consequence (breakout_1 can stop trading indefinitely with the only evidence being a journalctl line), rather than being left looking like a fix about to happen.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-PROP-SIZING-REFUSAL-ON-A-STALE-BALANCE-IS-JOURNALED-BUT-NEVER-PINGED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-PROP-SIZING-REFUSAL-ON-A-STALE-BALANCE-IS-JOURNALED-BUT-NEVER-PINGED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-PROP-SIZING-REFUSAL-ON-A-STALE-BALANCE-IS-JOURNALED-BUT-NEVER-PINGED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A prop account blocked from trading by a stale balance stops trading with NO operator-facing signal — the refusal is journaled and logged, and the ping that exists for exactly this is on a different branch"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A read surface reports, PER ACCOUNT, the set of venue books its credentials can actually reach -- the product categories queried AND the UID(s) answering -- beside the set the account DECLARES it trades, with a three-state verdict per account that never collapses 'covered' with 'we did not look': observed on the live fleet via a diag read, not from a test fixture. CLEARED when that surface returns a verdict for all 3 Bybit accounts AND at least one account grades something other than 'covered' or the all-covered verdict is confirmed against a positive control (an account deliberately queried on a category it does not trade must grade uncovered, proving the check can fail). NOT SUFFICIENT: a green unit test (a fixture cannot establish which books a real key reaches); the current reads returning rows (that is the assumption under test, not evidence for it); or the operator confirming where their position was (that answers THIS incident and leaves the class unmeasured).", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-NOTHING-VERIFIES-THAT-THE-BOOKS-OUR-KEYS-CAN-READ-ARE-ALL-THE-BOOKS-THE-CAPITAL-IS-ON", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-NOTHING-VERIFIES-THAT-THE-BOOKS-OUR-KEYS-CAN-READ-ARE-ALL-THE-BOOKS-THE-CAPITAL-IS-ON", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-NOTHING-VERIFIES-THAT-THE-BOOKS-OUR-KEYS-CAN-READ-ARE-ALL-THE-BOOKS-THE-CAPITAL-IS-ON'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Every venue read is scoped to category=linear and one UID per account, and NOTHING verifies that scope covers all the books the account's capital is actually on"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "check_pr_landing (or a sibling CI step) READS the PR's live auto-merge state — not the arming file — and FAILS when auto_merge is enabled while the landing declaration says hold, or while R4/R5 refuse self-landing. Verified by a POSITIVE CONTROL, because the whole defect is a check that passes on a state it cannot see: arm a scratch PR, let the workflow enable auto-merge, remove the arming file and declare hold, and observe the guard FAIL — a guard that stays green there has not been fixed, it has been re-verified as blind. NOT SUFFICIENT: removing the arming file (the observed no-op); a green run on a PR that was never armed (it cannot distinguish the fix from the defect); or documenting the two-push order in prose — that guidance ALREADY exists in CLAUDE.md and was violated six times in two days, which is why this needs a mechanism rather than a reminder.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-REMOVING-THE-ARMING-FILE-DOES-NOT-DISARM-AUTO-MERGE-GITHUB-HAS-ALREADY-ENABLED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-REMOVING-THE-ARMING-FILE-DOES-NOT-DISARM-AUTO-MERGE-GITHUB-HAS-ALREADY-ENABLED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-REMOVING-THE-ARMING-FILE-DOES-NOT-DISARM-AUTO-MERGE-GITHUB-HAS-ALREADY-ENABLED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] pr-landing R10 grades the ARMING FILE, but auto-merge GitHub has already enabled SURVIVES the file's removal — so a PR can be declared `hold` and still auto-merge"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A read surface reports, per OPEN journal row on a netted Bybit symbol, whether THAT ROW's own tracked leg ids (trades.sl_order_id / tp_order_id) are still resting at the venue -- not whether the SYMBOL is covered in aggregate. CLEARED when that surface is observed on the live fleet distinguishing at least two rows on one netted symbol, at least one of which has a resting own-leg and one of which does not, OR when a measurement over the journal establishes the population of rows that have EVER been open without an own-leg while a sibling's leg rested (a count, with the classifier stated and a positive control). NOT SUFFICIENT: the existing symbol-level covered_qty grade (it is the thing under test); a green unit test (a fixture cannot establish venue leg residency); or the observation that 5471 was alone (that refutes the hypothesis for ONE trade and says nothing about the class). ANY CHANGE TO THE COVERAGE BASIS ITSELF IS TIER-2 and must be proposed, not shipped.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260909-UNDER-NETTING-A-JOURNAL-ROW-CAN-BE-MASKED-BY-A-SIBLINGS-PROTECTIVE-LEG-AND-NOTHING-GRADES-PER-ROW-COVERAGE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-UNDER-NETTING-A-JOURNAL-ROW-CAN-BE-MASKED-BY-A-SIBLINGS-PROTECTIVE-LEG-AND-NOTHING-GRADES-PER-ROW-COVERAGE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-UNDER-NETTING-A-JOURNAL-ROW-CAN-BE-MASKED-BY-A-SIBLINGS-PROTECTIVE-LEG-AND-NOTHING-GRADES-PER-ROW-COVERAGE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Under Bybit netting one exchange position backs N journal rows, so a sibling's Partial leg can make