{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A PR opened by claude-pr-automerge under GITHUB_TOKEN is OBSERVED carrying real CI -- i.e. get_check_runs on a bot-opened PR returns the repo's actual required checks (guards, pytest-collect, pytest-run, repo-inventory) and not only `open-and-automerge` -- OR the workflow is observed REFUSING to create a PR at all (adopt-only), so the zero-CI birth is unreachable by construction. Name the PR and paste the check-run census. !! A QUIET WEEK CLEARS NOTHING: the trap fires only when the workflow WINS the race against a session's own create_pull_request, so an absence of occurrences is not evidence the shape is gone -- it went 2026-09-08 (six) to 2026-09-10 (one) with no code change in between. !! RESTATING THE ORDERING RULE ANYWHERE CLEARS NOTHING: that is what already exists at CLAUDE.md line ~1522 and what seven occurrences falsify. !! AND ONE SESSION FOLLOWING THE TWO-PUSH ORDER CORRECTLY (as PR #11700 did) IS NOT A FIX -- it is one session, and the row is about the default.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260910-CLAUDE-PR-AUTOMERGE-ORDERING-TRAP-RECURS-A-SEVENTH-TIME-BECAUSE-THE-REMEDY-IS-AN-ORDERING-RULE-WHOSE-VIOLATION-IS-THE-DEFAULT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260910-CLAUDE-PR-AUTOMERGE-ORDERING-TRAP-RECURS-A-SEVENTH-TIME-BECAUSE-THE-REMEDY-IS-AN-ORDERING-RULE-WHOSE-VIOLATION-IS-THE-DEFAULT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260910-CLAUDE-PR-AUTOMERGE-ORDERING-TRAP-RECURS-A-SEVENTH-TIME-BECAUSE-THE-REMEDY-IS-AN-ORDERING-RULE-WHOSE-VIOLATION-IS-THE-DEFAULT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] RECURRENCE (7th): a PR born under GITHUB_TOKEN carries ONE GREEN check and no real CI -- documented in CLAUDE.md, hit anyway, because the remedy is a two-push ordering rule"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "EITHER (a) api-contract.mjs distinguishes a field the consumer reads that is present in the fixture but NOT in a payload captured from the CURRENTLY DEPLOYED bot -- which needs the checker to know a live-capture provenance stamp, so the honest minimum is that a fixture declares whether it was captured from a deployed or a patched bot and the checker REPORTS that rather than passing silently; OR (b) it is recorded as a DECISION that the checker deliberately validates only the post-deploy contract, with the consequence stated -- that every cross-repo field addition must handle its own absence -- and that duty written where an author of such a pair will read it. !! A GREEN RUN CLEARS NOTHING: green is precisely what this row records as uninformative. !! AND FIXING THE ONE FIXTURE CLEARS NOTHING EITHER -- the MI-254 fixture is correct and honest; the gap is that nothing generalises it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260910-API-CONTRACT-FIXTURE-CAN-BE-AHEAD-OF-THE-DEPLOYED-BOT-SO-IT-CANNOT-CATCH-A-CONSUMER-READING-A-FIELD-NOTHING-SERVES-YET", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260910-API-CONTRACT-FIXTURE-CAN-BE-AHEAD-OF-THE-DEPLOYED-BOT-SO-IT-CANNOT-CATCH-A-CONSUMER-READING-A-FIELD-NOTHING-SERVES-YET", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260910-API-CONTRACT-FIXTURE-CAN-BE-AHEAD-OF-THE-DEPLOYED-BOT-SO-IT-CANNOT-CATCH-A-CONSUMER-READING-A-FIELD-NOTHING-SERVES-YET'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] webapp/tests/api-contract.mjs validates SPA field reads against a RECORDED fixture, which is routinely captured from a locally-patched bot -- so it passes on a field the DEPLOYED bot does not serve, and cannot see the pre-deploy window in which every row reading that field renders as a false negative"}
