{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A Data Explorer load in the DEPLOYED SPA returns 200 with real rows, observed on the live page. TWO INDEPENDENT PRECONDITIONS MUST BOTH HOLD and neither substitutes for the other: (1) the host can mint -- POST /api/auth/login with a WELL-FORMED body returns 401 invalid_credentials rather than 500 auth_unavailable, i.e. JWT_SIGNING_KEY / ALLOWED_EMAIL / WEBAPP_PASSWORD_SHA256 are set (Tier-2, operator originates the values); and (2) the SPA can SEND a bearer -- a login screen and token store exist in benbaichmankass/ict-trader-dashboard, which the gating commit measured as ABSENT. !! NOT sufficient: setting the envs alone -- that clears (1) and says nothing about (2). !! NOT sufficient: any test suite -- #11517 ships 34 passing tests and a harness cannot reach a deployed front end. !! NOT sufficient: an unauthenticated 401 from /api/bot/db/* -- that is the gate WORKING and is byte-identical in the healthy and broken states. !! AND A 422 FROM AN EMPTY LOGIN BODY IS NOT EVIDENCE EITHER WAY: Pydantic validation runs before the handler. Use a well-formed body. !! IF THE OPERATOR DECIDES the Data Explorer should stay closed -- legitimate, since failing closed on the money DB is the right side to err on -- this row does NOT clear, it CHANGES: the tab is then deliberately retired and that must be RECORDED as a decision rather than left looking like an outage about to be fixed.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-DB-EXPLORER-GATE-MERGED-WITH-BOTH-ITS-OWN-HELD-PRECONDITIONS-MEASURED-FALSE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-DB-EXPLORER-GATE-MERGED-WITH-BOTH-ITS-OWN-HELD-PRECONDITIONS-MEASURED-FALSE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-DB-EXPLORER-GATE-MERGED-WITH-BOTH-ITS-OWN-HELD-PRECONDITIONS-MEASURED-FALSE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] CONFIRMED BROKEN: the SPA's Data Explorer has been unreachable on the live host since 2026-09-09 — the /api/bot/db/* gate fails closed (correctly) and the host cannot mint a session, a documented precondition that was never closed"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A CLAUDE.md merge resolution can no longer silently drop non-brief content. Either the documented pattern changes to 'take main's copy of the GENERATED BLOCK ONLY, then diff the remainder against BOTH sides and resolve it as a union' -- written where the resolvers actually read it, i.e. the merge-driver docs and the manager cadence guidance, not only in a backlog row -- or a check compares the post-resolution CLAUDE.md against the branch's pre-merge copy OUTSIDE the generated block and refuses a net deletion the author did not make. [!] `render_session_brief.py --check` PASSING RESOLVES NOTHING and is what gave the false confidence: it grades the generated block and is blind to the rest of the file BY DESIGN. Do not extend it to cover this; that would conflate two different questions. [!] AND A WRITTEN WARNING ALONE IS NOT A MECHANISM -- this repo's own rules say so, and I applied a pattern I had used correctly before. What failed was not knowledge.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-TAKING-MAINS-CLAUDE-MD-WHOLESALE-TO-RESOLVE-A-SESSION-BRIEF-CONFLICT-SILENTLY-DROPS-THE-BRANCHS-OWN-HAND-WRITTEN-EDITS-TO-THAT-FILE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-TAKING-MAINS-CLAUDE-MD-WHOLESALE-TO-RESOLVE-A-SESSION-BRIEF-CONFLICT-SILENTLY-DROPS-THE-BRANCHS-OWN-HAND-WRITTEN-EDITS-TO-THAT-FILE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-TAKING-MAINS-CLAUDE-MD-WHOLESALE-TO-RESOLVE-A-SESSION-BRIEF-CONFLICT-SILENTLY-DROPS-THE-BRANCHS-OWN-HAND-WRITTEN-EDITS-TO-THAT-FILE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The documented CLAUDE.md conflict resolution — take main's copy wholesale, re-render the brief — silently DELETES any hand-written CLAUDE.md content the branch added; it cost an env-table row on a Tier-2 PR"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A ticket left in expiry_prompted (or any other prompted state) can no longer suppress the sleeve indefinitely. Concretely, EITHER: (a) prompted states carry a TIMEOUT after which the ticket auto-resolves to `expired` and stops counting as outstanding -- observed by finding such an auto-resolution in the live prop_tickets table, not by reading the code; OR (b) a detector PAGES the operator when any ticket has been in a prompted state beyond a threshold AND tickets are being suppressed against it -- observed firing on a real instance. [!] CLEARING THE TWO CURRENT TICKETS RESOLVES THIS NOT AT ALL -- that is the incident, and it is already done. [!] THE SLEEVE TRADING AGAIN IS NOT EVIDENCE EITHER: it will trade again the moment the jam clears, which says nothing about the next jam. [!] A GREEN TEST CLEARS NOTHING: the condition is a prompt a human did not answer, which a harness cannot reach. [!] AND DO NOT 'FIX' THIS BY MAKING THE RETICKET CHECK IGNORE expiry_prompted -- that check exists to stop duplicate tickets going to a human executor, and disabling it would trade a silent outage for silent double-placement on a real-money prop account. The fix belongs in the ticket's own lifecycle.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-ONE-UNANSWERED-EXPIRY-PROMPT-WEDGES-THE-ENTIRE-PROP-SLEEVE-FOREVER-WITH-NO-TIMEOUT-NO-ESCALATION-AND-NO-ALARM", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-ONE-UNANSWERED-EXPIRY-PROMPT-WEDGES-THE-ENTIRE-PROP-SLEEVE-FOREVER-WITH-NO-TIMEOUT-NO-ESCALATION-AND-NO-ALARM", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-ONE-UNANSWERED-EXPIRY-PROMPT-WEDGES-THE-ENTIRE-PROP-SLEEVE-FOREVER-WITH-NO-TIMEOUT-NO-ESCALATION-AND-NO-ALARM'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] One unanswered prop expiry-prompt suppressed EVERY prop ticket for 12 days, silently — expiry_prompted counts as an outstanding ticket and nothing ever clears it"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "EITHER (a) prop ticket sizing consults distance_to_dd_floor_usd and caps risk so that a single loss cannot take the account within one further loss of the floor -- observed on a real emitted ticket whose risk_usd is below the naive 1.5% figure BECAUSE of the floor, not because the balance fell; OR (b) the operator records a DECISION to accept the current sizing against the floor, with the two-losses-and-it-is-dead consequence stated in the decision itself. [!] A FRESH `bal` REPORT RESOLVES NOTHING HERE -- it fixes the freshness gate, which is a different row. If the new balance is higher the headroom grows and the arithmetic still has no guard. [!] AND THE ACCOUNT SURVIVING A TRADE IS NOT EVIDENCE: a winning trade says nothing about whether the sizing path can see the floor.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-PROP-TICKET-RISK-IS-75-DOLLARS-AGAINST-87-DOLLARS-OF-DRAWDOWN-FLOOR-SO-TWO-LOSSES-PERMANENTLY-DISABLE-THE-ACCOUNT", "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-PROP-TICKET-RISK-IS-75-DOLLARS-AGAINST-87-DOLLARS-OF-DRAWDOWN-FLOOR-SO-TWO-LOSSES-PERMANENTLY-DISABLE-THE-ACCOUNT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-PROP-TICKET-RISK-IS-75-DOLLARS-AGAINST-87-DOLLARS-OF-DRAWDOWN-FLOOR-SO-TWO-LOSSES-PERMANENTLY-DISABLE-THE-ACCOUNT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] breakout_1 sizes each ticket at ~$75 risk with $87.34 of static-drawdown headroom — two losing trades permanently disable the account, and nothing in the sizing path knows it"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "The answered-ness of a decision_request is readable ONE way. Either the two shapes are converged (with the losing shape migrated, not merely deprecated), or a single accessor owns the question and every consumer imports it -- the `src/runtime/provenance.py` pattern this repo already uses for 'is this pnl measured'. Verified by a guard that FAILS on an object carrying the other shape, with its own planted-defect self-test. [!] A DOC SAYING 'use the flat shape' RESOLVES NOTHING -- the repo's own rules record that documenting a convention is not a mechanism, and both shapes are already on main. [!] AND CONVERGING THE SCHEMA DOES NOT DISCHARGE DEFECT (2): that one is a session-discipline failure, already covered by RULE ONE, and is recorded here as a worked instance rather than as a thing to fix in code.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-DECISION-REQUESTS-CARRY-TWO-INCOMPATIBLE-ANSWER-SCHEMAS-SO-A-PROBE-KEYED-ON-ONE-REPORTS-ANSWERED-DECISIONS-AS-OPEN", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-DECISION-REQUESTS-CARRY-TWO-INCOMPATIBLE-ANSWER-SCHEMAS-SO-A-PROBE-KEYED-ON-ONE-REPORTS-ANSWERED-DECISIONS-AS-OPEN", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-DECISION-REQUESTS-CARRY-TWO-INCOMPATIBLE-ANSWER-SCHEMAS-SO-A-PROBE-KEYED-ON-ONE-REPORTS-ANSWERED-DECISIONS-AS-OPEN'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] decision_requests answers live in TWO schemas (flat chosen/verdict vs nested answer:) — a probe keyed on one reports settled decisions as unanswered; measured flat=3 nested=25 unanswered=0"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "The 2026-08-30 break is ATTRIBUTED: a session states which candidate it established, how, and over what population, and the e35 half is either reverted or cleared. The discriminating measurement above is run and its verdict recorded, which also discharges OI-20260830-E35-GEOMETRY-SHIPPED-TO-9-LEGS-NOT-YET-LIVE-VERIFIED. [!] 'THE MARKET CHOPPED' IS NOT A VERDICT UNLESS MEASURED -- it is the comfortable answer and needs the SAME evidence: the non-e35 control degrading equally. Asserting regime without the control is how a real parameter defect gets absorbed as weather. [!] PROFITABILITY RETURNING RESOLVES NOTHING -- the cause would stay unknown and the next occurrence just as invisible. [!] NOR DOES REVERTING e35 ALONE: without the control we never learn whether it was the cause, and ict_scalp_* stays unexplained. [!] AND A SEPARATE CLAUSE THAT MUST NOT BE FOLDED IN: nothing alarmed on fifteen consecutive losing days. A sustained per-book losing-streak detector is owed whatever the attribution turns out to be.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-A-DATED-REGIME-BREAK-ON-2026-08-30-COLLAPSED-THE-DIRECTIONAL-LEGS-WIN-RATE-AND-NOBODY-NOTICED-FOR-TWO-WEEKS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-A-DATED-REGIME-BREAK-ON-2026-08-30-COLLAPSED-THE-DIRECTIONAL-LEGS-WIN-RATE-AND-NOBODY-NOTICED-FOR-TWO-WEEKS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-A-DATED-REGIME-BREAK-ON-2026-08-30-COLLAPSED-THE-DIRECTIONAL-LEGS-WIN-RATE-AND-NOBODY-NOTICED-FOR-TWO-WEEKS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Directional legs broke on 2026-08-30 — trend_donchian win rate 74.1% → 12.9%, ict_scalp 54.7% → 31.8%, bybit_1 has had FIFTEEN consecutive losing days, and no review or monitor raised it"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "THE FIX IS TIER-2 (it changes what pages a live operator) AND IS NOT APPLIED HERE. What it needs: _residual_from_positions must compare the symbol's net book against what the journal's REMAINING OPEN rows on that (account, symbol, side) account for, and report a violation only on the UNATTRIBUTED excess — the same attribution _reconcile_netting_partial_closes already performs for bybit. Equivalently and more cheaply as a first cut: suppress the violation when open sibling rows on that (account, symbol, side) sum to >= the observed net, since then nothing is unaccounted for.\n\n⚠️ A FOURTH STATE IS REQUIRED, NOT A BOOLEAN: 'net is fully accounted for by open siblings' / 'net exceeds what the siblings account for' (the real finding) / 'we could not read the sibling rows' (NEVER folded into either) — beside the existing flat/residual/could_not_look. Collapsing 'we could not attribute' into 'flat' would re-create F-11, the exact defect this module was repaired to stop having.\n\nCLEARS WHEN: a close on a netted symbol WITH open siblings is observed producing NO violation, AND a genuine unattributed residual is still reported — both halves, because a fix that merely silences the alarm is indistinguishable from one that works, and this module's 14.7-day zero is precisely what that looks like. ⚠️ A GREEN TEST CLEARS NOTHING: run_residual_controls() plants a single-position book and passes today while the live rows are wrong, because the control never constructs a multi-sibling netted bo …[truncated]", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-GRADES-THE-SYMBOL-NET-BOOK-NOT-THE-CLOSING-TRADE-SO-EVERY-NETTED-CLOSE-WITH-OPEN-SIBLINGS-IS-A-FALSE-ERROR-PAGE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-GRADES-THE-SYMBOL-NET-BOOK-NOT-THE-CLOSING-TRADE-SO-EVERY-NETTED-CLOSE-WITH-OPEN-SIBLINGS-IS-A-FALSE-ERROR-PAGE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-CLOSED-FLAT-INVARIANT-GRADES-THE-SYMBOL-NET-BOOK-NOT-THE-CLOSING-TRADE-SO-EVERY-NETTED-CLOSE-WITH-OPEN-SIBLINGS-IS-A-FALSE-ERROR-PAGE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] closed-flat invariant reports the account+symbol NET position as the closing trade's residual, so on a netting account every close with open siblings is a FALSE violation — 9 false Level.ERROR pages to the operator since 2026-09-10, and the falsifier that 'can finally speak' is saying something untrue"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, different facts — say WHICH was cleared. (1) A SCHEDULED run of replay-pregate-nightly.yml concludes success AND runtime_logs/replay_pregate/ is non-empty on origin/main carrying that run's artifact. Read the run history and the committed file, never the workflow yaml. (2) The push route is fixed so a run cannot silently discard partial evidence: it must not push straight at protected main with no rebase/retry — route it through .github/actions/commit-to-main like the other producers (⚠️ but see BL-20260911-THE-SHARED-COMMIT-TO-MAIN-LANDING-STEP-IS-THE-LARGEST-SINGLE-CAUSE-OF-DISCARDED-AUTOMATION-OUTPUT first — that path has its own failure mode and porting onto it blind trades one loss for another).\n\n⚠️ A GREEN workflow_dispatch RUN CLEARS NOTHING: the failure class is a nightly cadence that has never once delivered, and dispatch is not that. ⚠️ AND THE DIRECTORY BECOMING NON-EMPTY BY A HAND-COMMIT CLEARS NOTHING EITHER — the artifact must come from a scheduled run.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-REPLAY-PREGATE-NIGHTLY-HAS-ZERO-SUCCESSFUL-RUNS-IN-ITS-ENTIRE-LIFE-AND-25-MONTHS-OF-ML-PREGATE-EVIDENCE-HAS-ACCRUED-TO-NOTHING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-REPLAY-PREGATE-NIGHTLY-HAS-ZERO-SUCCESSFUL-RUNS-IN-ITS-ENTIRE-LIFE-AND-25-MONTHS-OF-ML-PREGATE-EVIDENCE-HAS-ACCRUED-TO-NOTHING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-REPLAY-PREGATE-NIGHTLY-HAS-ZERO-SUCCESSFUL-RUNS-IN-ITS-ENTIRE-LIFE-AND-25-MONTHS-OF-ML-PREGATE-EVIDENCE-HAS-ACCRUED-TO-NOTHING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] replay-pregate-nightly.yml: 77 scheduled runs, 68 failure / 9 cancelled / ZERO success ever, on any event — two and a half months of nightly ML pre-gate evidence accrued to an empty directory and nothing alarmed"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A SCHEDULED run of sunset-pass.yml completes AND its artifact is on origin/main carrying that run's stamp. Read the run history and the committed file. ⚠️ A workflow_dispatch run clears the PUSH-ROUTE question only and must be recorded as such — the failure class being watched is a weekly cadence that has never delivered. ⚠️ IF THE OPERATOR DECIDES the sunset pass should not run weekly, this does NOT clear — it CHANGES: the sunset list is then produced by nothing on a cadence, which is a legitimate decision and must be RECORDED as one rather than left looking like a cadence about to start, AND the SESSION BRIEF's sunset block must stop presenting the stale candidates as current.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-SUNSET-PASS-PUSHES-STRAIGHT-AT-PROTECTED-MAIN-SO-ITS-ONLY-SCHEDULED-RUN-COULD-NOT-LAND-AND-IT-WILL-FAIL-IDENTICALLY-EVERY-MONDAY", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-SUNSET-PASS-PUSHES-STRAIGHT-AT-PROTECTED-MAIN-SO-ITS-ONLY-SCHEDULED-RUN-COULD-NOT-LAND-AND-IT-WILL-FAIL-IDENTICALLY-EVERY-MONDAY", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-SUNSET-PASS-PUSHES-STRAIGHT-AT-PROTECTED-MAIN-SO-ITS-ONLY-SCHEDULED-RUN-COULD-NOT-LAND-AND-IT-WILL-FAIL-IDENTICALLY-EVERY-MONDAY'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] sunset-pass.yml pushes directly at protected main and is declined by the branch-protection hook — its ONE scheduled run failed, it will recur every Monday, and the SESSION BRIEF is advertising 10 sunset candidates from a pass that never landed"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "The landing step distinguishes and survives its two failure modes. Concretely: (a) a generated-artifact PR that conflicts because main moved is REGENERATED against the new main and retried, rather than timing out and being closed — an artifact recomputable from main is exactly the case where rebase-and-retry is safe; and (b) a rate-limit refusal is retried with backoff past the window rather than consuming the run, AND is reported DISTINGUISHABLY from a substantive failure so that a red pr-queue-watch means the queue is unworked and nothing else.\n\nCLEARS WHEN: a scheduled run is observed hitting one of these conditions and still landing its artifact on main — read the run log and the committed file. ⚠️ A QUIET WEEK CLEARS NOTHING: both sub-causes need main to be busy (or GitHub to be throttling) to arise at all, so an absence of failures may mean the condition did not occur. Establish that artifacts were being produced across the window before reading zero losses as a fix. ⚠️ AND CLOSING THE CONFLICTED PRs BY HAND, however well-reasoned, IS NOT A FIX — that is what has been happening and the cadence regenerates the loss.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-THE-SHARED-COMMIT-TO-MAIN-LANDING-STEP-IS-THE-LARGEST-SINGLE-CAUSE-OF-DISCARDED-AUTOMATION-OUTPUT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-THE-SHARED-COMMIT-TO-MAIN-LANDING-STEP-IS-THE-LARGEST-SINGLE-CAUSE-OF-DISCARDED-AUTOMATION-OUTPUT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-THE-SHARED-COMMIT-TO-MAIN-LANDING-STEP-IS-THE-LARGEST-SINGLE-CAUSE-OF-DISCARDED-AUTOMATION-OUTPUT'), indent=2))\""}, 