{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "The tolerance is re-derived from MEASURED reconciler fill dispersion rather than chosen, with the population stated, OR exit location is adjudicated from the price path where candles are available and the two instruments are reported side by side. [!] SIMPLY WIDENING THE BAND IS NOT SUFFICIENT AND IS DANGEROUS IN THE OTHER DIRECTION: a wider band makes a `neither` exit near a bracket read as a stop-out, which would inflate every stop rate in the repo. Measure the dispersion first. [!] AND NOTE MI-271's POSITIVE CONTROL WAS NOT WRONG -- 88.4% recall means ~12% missed, and this row is that 12% located rather than a new defect.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-EXIT-ADJUDICATION-AT-15BP-MISSES-STOP-OUTS-WHOSE-RECONCILER-FILL-LANDS-OUTSIDE-THE-BAND", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-EXIT-ADJUDICATION-AT-15BP-MISSES-STOP-OUTS-WHOSE-RECONCILER-FILL-LANDS-OUTSIDE-THE-BAND", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-EXIT-ADJUDICATION-AT-15BP-MISSES-STOP-OUTS-WHOSE-RECONCILER-FILL-LANDS-OUTSIDE-THE-BAND'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] MI-271's exit adjudicator uses a 15bp touch band and misses stop-outs whose reconciler fill lands outside it; 2 of 33 packages measured"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "MFE/MAE in ATR units is computed per leg per week on a durable surface and a session is OBSERVED reading it. [!] DO NOT BUILD IT ON THIS ROW ALONE WITHOUT CHECKING MI-276 (WO-20260911-NOTHING-ALARMED-ON-EITHER-FAILURE-THE-SUSTAINED), which owns the losing-streak detector for the same incident -- two cadences landing in the same window is how they come to disagree. THEY ARE COMPLEMENTS, NOT DUPLICATES: a streak detector says THAT the book is bleeding, this says WHY, and it needs no provenance-clean PnL, which is what made the streak question hard. [!] AND IT NEEDS CANDLES, which the trader has and the repo's offline surfaces mostly do not -- cost the fetch before promising a cadence. [!] A QUIET READING IS NOT EVIDENCE OF HEALTH until the ratio has been seen MOVING on a known event; this window is the known event to validate it against.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-MFE-OVER-MAE-IN-ATR-UNITS-IS-A-LEADING-INDICATOR-NOBODY-COMPUTES", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-MFE-OVER-MAE-IN-ATR-UNITS-IS-A-LEADING-INDICATOR-NOBODY-COMPUTES", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-MFE-OVER-MAE-IN-ATR-UNITS-IS-A-LEADING-INDICATOR-NOBODY-COMPUTES'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] Favourable:adverse excursion in ATR units fell from 1.0-4.6 to 0.33-0.54 across 2026-08-30 and no surface computes it"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A FIELD-LEVEL loss proof exists as a committed, re-runnable script (not a throwaway in one session's context -- the sibling row names that as explicitly insufficient) and is OBSERVED failing on a deliberately-reverted test row. Its shape, because this is the part that matters: for every id present in either parent, compare the merge result against BOTH parents and the merge base, and FAIL when a side that changed a field is not carried -- including the two cases an id-set check cannot express, `result == ours and result != theirs` and the reverse. [!] AN ID-SET / ROW-COUNT CHECK DOES NOT SATISFY THIS and must stop being cited as a merge proof; it passed on the very merge that lost three rows' edits. [!] A TYPE-CHANGE GUARD DOES NOT SATISFY THIS EITHER -- see why_it_matters; no type changed here. [!] NOR DOES merge.jsonregister BEING ARMED: it WAS armed, the file IS covered by it, and the loss happened anyway at the point the conflicted result was staged. Whether the driver refused and the staging overrode it, or the driver resolved it badly, is NOT established here and is worth establishing before anyone relies on the driver as the protection. [!] AND DO NOT CLOSE THIS BY FIXING THE THREE ROWS -- they are already repaired on claude/mi275-stop-width-counterfactual by a field-level union that carries both sides, verified. The open defect is that nothing but an ad-hoc check caught it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-A-UNION-BY-ID-SET-PROOF-IS-BLIND-TO-A-MERGE-THAT-DROPS-A-FIELD-AND-IT-IS-THE-REMEDY-EVERY-LANE-IS-TOLD-TO-USE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-A-UNION-BY-ID-SET-PROOF-IS-BLIND-TO-A-MERGE-THAT-DROPS-A-FIELD-AND-IT-IS-THE-REMEDY-EVERY-LANE-IS-TOLD-TO-USE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-A-UNION-BY-ID-SET-PROOF-IS-BLIND-TO-A-MERGE-THAT-DROPS-A-FIELD-AND-IT-IS-THE-REMEDY-EVERY-LANE-IS-TOLD-TO-USE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] RECURRENCE of BL-20260909: a union-by-ID-SET merge proof passed 225/225/225 while three SESSIONS.json rows silently lost the other side's edits — and id-set union is the remedy the board tells every lane to use"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 45, "clears_when": "ONE of the following, and the first is preferred because it removes the ambiguity rather than documenting it. (a) coverage() distinguishes the two cases -- e.g. it RAISES (or returns a distinct sentinel) when 'total' is absent from a non-empty counts mapping, so a wiring error fails loud instead of rendering as caution, while a genuinely empty window still returns None. (b) coverage() derives the denominator from the four bucket counts when 'total' is absent, making the key optional rather than load-bearing. (c) The operator/owner decides the explicit-total contract is correct and it is RECORDED, with split_counts named in the docstring as the required producer and the hand-built path called out as unsupported. !! WHICHEVER IS CHOSEN, THE None-MEANS-EMPTY-WINDOW SEMANTICS MUST SURVIVE IT -- collapsing that back into 0.0 would undo the distinction the module exists for and is a strictly worse outcome than the bug being fixed. !! AND ANY CHANGE NEEDS THE EXISTING CONSUMERS RE-READ: performance.py, shadow.py and _pnl_provenance.py all render coverage to an operator-facing surface, so a new raising path must not be able to 5xx a read route.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260911-PROVENANCE-COVERAGE-READS-A-CALLERS-MISSING-TOTAL-KEY-AS-NO-DENOMINATOR", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260911-PROVENANCE-COVERAGE-READS-A-CALLERS-MISSING-TOTAL-KEY-AS-NO-DENOMINATOR", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260911-PROVENANCE-COVERAGE-READS-A-CALLERS-MISSING-TOTAL-KEY-AS-NO-DENOMINATOR'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] provenance.coverage() keys 