{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A stuck-branch report is OBSERVED on a surface a session reaches without being told to look — a committed receipt whose generated_at comes from a run whose EVENT is `schedule` (read the run history, never the file's existence, because a workflow_dispatch writes a byte-identical artifact), or a due-list source that grades the count. [!] THE PROBE PASSING ITS --self-test CLEARS NOTHING: it has always passed, and the 181 branches were invisible throughout — the defect is the absent CALLER, not the probe. [!] A ONE-OFF MANUAL RUN CLEARS NOTHING EITHER: that is exactly what produced the 181 figure, and it is the state this row describes. [!] THE REPORT MUST PAGE ON A TRANSITION, NOT ON THE STANDING COUNT — 181 rows every run is the desensitised alarm this repo already pays for, so a carrier that re-reports the backlog every time is not a pass. [!] AND IF THE OPERATOR DECIDES STRANDED AUTOMATION BRANCHES ARE NOT WORTH A CARRIER, this row does not clear — it CHANGES: record that as a decision with its consequence stated (the count keeps growing and nobody sees it) rather than leaving it looking like a carrier about to be built. [!] STILL OWED AS OF 2026-09-12: exactly the scheduled-run observation above. The carrier is deployed, not proven, and the `probes` cron is `20 5 * * *` — which this repo has measured firing ~4h50m LATE, so read the run history rather than the clock.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260912-THE-STUCK-BRANCH-PROBE-IS-WIRED-TO-NOTHING-SO-181-STRANDED-AUTOMATION-BRANCHES-ARE-SEEN-BY-NOBODY", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260912-THE-STUCK-BRANCH-PROBE-IS-WIRED-TO-NOTHING-SO-181-STRANDED-AUTOMATION-BRANCHES-ARE-SEEN-BY-NOBODY", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260912-THE-STUCK-BRANCH-PROBE-IS-WIRED-TO-NOTHING-SO-181-STRANDED-AUTOMATION-BRANCHES-ARE-SEEN-BY-NOBODY'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] stuck_automation_branches.py runs on nobody's schedule while 181 automation branches sit stranded"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "THREE PARTS, different facts -- say WHICH you cleared. (1) THE READ IS COMPLETE: a bybit_2 position_read_state_soak row shows rows_seen covering every book the venue holds, verified against an independent venue read taken the same minute, on a symbol carrying TWO non-zero hedge books. !! A row where the venue happens to hold one book per symbol proves nothing -- establish the two-book case exists in the window before reading any pass. (2) could_not_look IS EXPRESSIBLE: a read that did not fetch a symbol's second book increments could_not_look_count rather than silently reading 0, so the instrument can report its own blindness. (3) OBSERVED ON THE FLEET: the previously-invisible book appears in /api/bot/positions and on the dashboard, and the naked-protection sweep is observed GRADING it. !! MI-283's dedupe fix (PR #11903) CLEARS NONE OF THIS -- it is a correct fix for a DIFFERENT path (bybit_1, 148/148) and this row must not be closed by its merge. !! A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING: a fixture cannot reproduce a venue page returning fewer rows than the account holds, which IS the mechanism. !! AND THE LIVE POSITION'S CONTAINMENT IS A SEPARATE FACT from the code fix: if the operator flattens or brackets it manually, that settles the money at risk and clears NONE of (1)-(3).", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260912-BYBIT2-SETTLE-COIN-PAGE-RETURNS-FEWER-POSITIONS-THAN-THE-VENUE-HOLDS-SO-A-REAL-MONEY-HEDGE-BOOK-IS-NEVER-FETCHED-AND-SITS-NAKED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260912-BYBIT2-SETTLE-COIN-PAGE-RETURNS-FEWER-POSITIONS-THAN-THE-VENUE-HOLDS-SO-A-REAL-MONEY-HEDGE-BOOK-IS-NEVER-FETCHED-AND-SITS-NAKED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260912-BYBIT2-SETTLE-COIN-PAGE-RETURNS-FEWER-POSITIONS-THAN-THE-VENUE-HOLDS-SO-A-REAL-MONEY-HEDGE-BOOK-IS-NEVER-FETCHED-AND-SITS-NAKED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] OPERATOR-RAISED 2026-09-12T08:0xZ. A REAL-MONEY ETHUSDT SHORT 0.05 on bybit_2 is open on the venue with NO stop and NO take-profit, and is invisible to every bot surface. !! THE CAUSE IS NOT THE SYMBOL DEDUPE and must not be filed under it: measured over position_read_state_soak (400 rows, 2026-09-12T06:38:14->08:07:44), bybit_2 drops a deduped book on 0 of 145 reads, against bybit_1 at 148 of 148 (SOLUSDT idx1/idx2). The manager initially attributed it to the dedupe and was WRONG. THE ACTUAL MECHANISM, from a raw bybit_2 soak row: rows_seen 6, emitted 2, and queries = settle_coin_page -> row_count 2 (the venue holds THREE), then symbol_scoped BTCUSDT and ADAUSDT only. The symbol-scoped backfill runs only for symbols NOT already seen, so because ETHUSDT appeared once (the long, position_idx=1) no symbol-scoped ETHUSDT query is ever issued and the idx=2 short book is NEVER FETCHED. It is not dropped -- it is never read, which is why the dedupe counter is correctly zero. !! AND could_not_look_count READS 0: the reader cannot express that it failed to look, so a miss is indistinguishable from an empty book -- the collapsed state this repo has a guard class for. VENUE-SIDE CONFIRMATION (not inferred from the soak alone): /api/diag/bybit_open_orders?account_id=bybit_2 returns 4 resting orders, ALL reduce-only, and both ETH legs are side=Sell qty=0.03 -- they reduce the LONG. A short is closed by a BUY and there is no ETH Buy leg on the account, so the short is genuinely unprotected. JOURNAL: trade 5644 (short 0.05 @ 2411.19, trend_donchian_eth_4h) reads status=closed, exit_reason=sl, exit_price=2477.45, pnl=-3.4241, closed_at 2026-09-11T08:30:35Z, with pnl_source AND exit_price_source both None -- NO PROVENANCE -- while the venue never closed it; the close also cancelled its tracked sl_order_id/tp_order_id legs. So the position has been live and naked for ~24h. !! ENTRY IS 2411.19 IN THE JOURNAL vs 2411.70 ON THE OPERATOR'S TERMINAL: size, direction and account match exactly, so identity is NEAR-CERTAIN rather than proven, and that is stated rather than rounded away. !! WHY THE SETTLE-COIN PAGE RETURNS 2 OF 3 IS NOT ESTABLISHED -- that is Bybit behaviour this session holds no evidence on, and the row deliberately asserts no cause for it.\n\n=== 2026-09-13 (MI-279 OPS lane, U29) — RE-MEASURED 24h ON. THE MECHANISM IS UNCHANGED AND INVARIANT; WHETHER THE THIRD BOOK IS STILL THERE IS UNDETERMINED AND CANNOT BE DETERMINED WITH ANY SURFACE THIS REPO SHIPS. ===\nPOPULATION, stated because the invariance is the point: the newest 400 rows of position_read_state_soak (file 19,726,073 B), read 2026-09-13T07:49Z — 148 bybit_2 rows spanning 06:28:33Z -> 07:49:51Z, plus 148 bybit_1 and 104 bybit_portfolio rows as controls.\n(1) THE MECHANISM IS UNCHANGED AND PERFECTLY INVARIANT ON bybit_2. `settle_coin_page` returned row_count 2 on 148 of 148 reads — no variance at all. The symbol-scoped backfill fired for BTCUSDT (148/148) and ADAUSDT (148/148) and for NOTHING else: ETHUSDT symbol-scoped queries in the whole tail = 0 of 148, XRPUSDT = 0 of 148. `(rows_seen, emitted, could_not_look_count)` is `(6, 2, 0)` on all 148 rows. So the row's mechanism — a symbol that appears ONCE on the page is never read symbol-scoped, and its second hedge book is never fetched — is live, and the code has not changed (`git log --since=2026-09-11 -- src/units/accounts/clients.py` shows only 73747db45 / #11903, the MI-283 DEDUPE fix, which this row already says clears none of it).\n(2) POSITIVE CONTROL, so the zero above has a denominator: on bybit_1 the backfill IS alive — its page returns 8 or 9 rows and AVAXUSDT is read symbol-scoped in 105 of 148. The bybit_2 zero is therefore the condition, not dead code.\n(3) THE ACCOUNT IS DEMONSTRABLY IN HEDGE MODE, FROM THE VENUE RATHER THAN FROM AN ENV VAR. A non-zero `position_idx` exists only in hedge mode, and the live read shows ETHUSDT at idx 1 and XRPUSDT at idx 2; the two symbol-scoped backfills each returned 2 rows (idx1 + idx2, both size 0). So every symbol on this account can hold two books, and the page returns at most one row per symbol — which makes the exposure GENERAL to every page-listed symbol, not specific to ETH.\n(4) `could_not_look_count` IS STILL 0 ON EVERY ROW — criterion (2) is UNMET, and that collapsed state is exactly what makes (5) unanswerable.\n(5) IF THE SHORT STILL EXISTS IT IS STILL UNPROTECTED. `/api/diag/bybit_open_orders?account_id=bybit_2` at 07:49:53Z, read_state `orders_read`: FOUR resting orders, all reduce-only — ETHUSDT Sell 0.03 x2 (TP 2848.3 / SL 2503.5, which reduce the LONG) and XRPUSDT Buy 55.6 x2 (which reduce the short). There is still NO ETH Buy leg, and a short is closed by a BUY. Unchanged from the row's original finding, now ~48h.\n[!] AND HERE IS WHAT I WILL NOT CLAIM. `row_count 2` has TWO explanations that fit my data identically: (A) the page omits a third non-zero book — the row's claim, evidenced on 2026-09-12 by the OPERATOR'S TERMINAL showing three; or (B) the page returns exactly the non-zero books and there are now only two, i.e. the short was flattened between then and now. I cannot distinguish them, and neither can any bot surface, because every one of them reads through the defective path. Their silence is NOT evidence the position closed. THE STRUCTURAL DEFECT STANDS UNDER EITHER, since it is read out of the query list rather than inferred from a count.\n[!] CRITERION (1) IS UNREACHABLE FROM A SESSION WITH THE TOOLING THIS REPO SHIPS, AND THAT IS THE MOST USEFUL THING THIS PASS FOUND. It asks for the soak row to be verified against an independent venue read taken the same minute. There is no such read: `/api/diag/exchange_positions` (src/web/api/routers/diag.py::get_exchange_positions) takes `account_id` ONLY — no `symbol` parameter exists anywhere on the diag surface for positions. I appended `&symbol=ETHUSDT` and got a BYTE-IDENTICAL payload including XRPUSDT, i.e. the unknown parameter was accepted and silently ignored; a session that did not compare the two responses would have reported that as a symbol-scoped read and cleared the criterion on nothing. The one endpoint that does take `symbol` is `/api/diag/venue_session`, which answers a different question.\n[!] SO THE CHEAPEST THING THAT WOULD MAKE THIS ROW CLOSEABLE IS A READ-ONLY PARAMETER, NOT A FIX: `symbol=` on `/api/diag/exchange_positions`, forwarded to a symbol-scoped venue query, would let any session take exactly the independent read criterion (1) demands — and would have settled (A)-vs-(B) above in one call. It is `src/**` and therefore Tier-2 under this lane's dispatch, so it is PROPOSED and not taken.\n[!] THE FIX PROPOSAL, ROUTED NOT TAKEN (Tier-2, src/units/accounts/clients.py): the backfill condition is 'symbol NOT already seen', which is unsound on a hedge account because seeing one book is not seeing the symbol. It should be 'symbol not seen, OR the symbol is hedge-armed and fewer than 2 books came back', and a hedge-armed symbol yielding <2 books with no symbol-scoped read issued must increment `could_not_look_count` — which is criterion (2), and is what turns this from an invisible miss into a reportable one. Hedge-armed is readable from the venue (`position_idx != 0`) as well as from `BYBIT_HEDGE_MODE_SYMBOLS`, and the venue is the better source: CLAUDE.md's own row for that variable warns it has gone stale twice in one day.\n[!] ONE THING THAT DID CHANGE, RECORDED WITH ITS CAVEAT: bybit_1's dedupe drops are 0 of 148 in this window, against the row's measured 148 of 148 on 2026-09-12 (SOLUSDT idx1/idx2). #11903 merged in between, so that is consistent with the fix working — but it is ALSO consistent with the two-book SOL condition simply having ended, and I did not establish which. Do not score it as MI-283 verified."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "append_row PRINTS its top duplicate candidates on EVERY file, not only when one clears the refusal threshold -- so the filer sees a 0.544 near-miss and decides, which is the decision the docstring already asks them to make ('If it is a DUPLICATE, drop yours... If it is a RECURRENCE, say so'). The refusal threshold itself should NOT simply be lowered to 0.544: that number is one observation, and a lower refusal turns a near-miss into a hard block on legitimate sibling rows, which is worse than the current silence. Separating INFORM from REFUSE is what the evidence supports. VERIFIED BY: re-running the simulation in this row -- rebuild the backlog without BL-20260908-ALPACA-PROTECTIVE-COVERAGE-IS-GRADED-BY-SIDE-NEVER-BY-QUANTITY, file it, and assert the 0.544 candidate is SHOWN. A unit test over a fixture is not sufficient on its own, because the finding is about what a real 1499-row corpus scores; pin the real pair. NOT SUFFICIENT: raising or lowering SIMILAR_REFUSE_SCORE alone, or adding another override -- the filer being shown nothing is the defect, not the number.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260912-THE-DUPLICATE-PRE-CHECK-SCORES-A-CONFIRMED-DUPLICATE-AT-0-POINT-544-AGAINST-A-0-POINT-65-REFUSAL-SO-IT-ACCEPTS-IT-SILENTLY", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260912-THE-DUPLICATE-PRE-CHECK-SCORES-A-CONFIRMED-DUPLICATE-AT-0-POINT-544-AGAINST-A-0-POINT-65-REFUSAL-SO-IT-ACCEPTS-IT-SILENTLY", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260912-THE-DUPLICATE-PRE-CHECK-SCORES-A-CONFIRMED-DUPLICATE-AT-0-POINT-544-AGAINST-A-0-POINT-65-REFUSAL-SO-IT-ACCEPTS-IT-SILENTLY'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] append_row's duplicate pre-check scored a CONFIRMED duplicate at 0.544 against its 0.65 refusal threshold, so it accepted the row silently and showed the filer nothing — the anti-duplicate mechanism the operator asked for did not fire on the case it exists for"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "An open backlog row whose fix has already landed is SURFACED to a session by something other than that session happening to run `git log` on the right file — and the surfacing is OBSERVED acting at least once, naming which row and which landed change. [!] NOT satisfied by a memo, by a convention added to a skill, or by a reminder in CLAUDE.md: both instances here were produced by sessions that had read all of those. [!] NOT satisfied by a check that merely asks whether a fix CITES its row — instance (2) cited it three times and changed nothing. [!] AND NOT satisfied by bulk-flipping rows to `resolved`: in instance (2) `open` is the CORRECT status and what was missing is an in-place update, so a remedy that can only flip status would make the record worse while looking like progress.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260912-A-LANDED-FIX-LEAVES-ITS-BACKLOG-ROW-OPEN-SO-THE-ROW-RECRUITS-THE-NEXT-SESSION-INTO-REBUILDING-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260912-A-LANDED-FIX-LEAVES-ITS-BACKLOG-ROW-OPEN-SO-THE-ROW-RECRUITS-THE-NEXT-SESSION-INTO-REBUILDING-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260912-A-LANDED-FIX-LEAVES-ITS-BACKLOG-ROW-OPEN-SO-THE-ROW-RECRUITS-THE-NEXT-SESSION-INTO-REBUILDING-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A PR that fixes a finding does not update the row, so the row stays `open` — and an open row is not merely wrong, it actively recruits the next session into rebuilding what already exists"}
