{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A guard invoked DIRECTLY with --base on a dirty tree says so -- naming the uncommitted paths and which of them are inside the range it is about to grade -- and is OBSERVED doing it on a real invocation, not asserted from a diff. [!] THE COSTED REMEDY, so nobody re-derives it: there is NO shared guard library -- all 18 are standalone and stdlib-only (checked: none imports a first-party module), so the honest implementation is one small shared helper plus 18 call sites, which is a unit of its own and is why it is FILED here rather than half-done. run_guards.py::dirty_tree_lines is already PURE and says so in its docstring, so it is the function to reuse rather than reimplement. [!] IT MUST NOT SILENTLY FIX ANYTHING -- no stashing, no committing, no grading the worktree instead. The parent row's own criteria say this and the reason is that the committed-state reading is what CI does; changing it would make the local run disagree with CI, which is worse than the trap. A NOTICE ONLY. [!] A WRAPPER SCRIPT IS NOT SUFFICIENT and should not be proposed: nothing forces a session to type it, which is the exact reason the run_guards fix did not reach these four instances. [!] AND 'tell sessions to commit first' IS NOT SUFFICIENT EITHER -- that instruction already exists, I had read it, and I still did it four times in one session.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-THE-DIRTY-TREE-NOTICE-LIVES-ONLY-IN-RUN-GUARDS-SO-ALL-18-DIRECTLY-INVOCABLE-DIFF-SCOPED-GUARDS-STILL-GRADE-THE-WRONG-TREE-SILENTLY", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-THE-DIRTY-TREE-NOTICE-LIVES-ONLY-IN-RUN-GUARDS-SO-ALL-18-DIRECTLY-INVOCABLE-DIFF-SCOPED-GUARDS-STILL-GRADE-THE-WRONG-TREE-SILENTLY", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/register