{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A register-touching PR is OBSERVED sitting open across an hour boundary WITHOUT session-brief-guard reding on it. !! RE-RENDERING A PR AND SEEING IT GO GREEN CLOSES NOTHING -- that is the current behaviour and buys one hour; the claim is about what happens at the NEXT tick. !! AND IF THE DECISION IS TO KEEP THE HOUR COUNTER AS IS, that is a legitimate outcome and closes this row -- but it must be RECORDED as a decision, with the re-render treadmill accepted knowingly, rather than left looking like a defect nobody got to.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-THE-RENDERED-SESSION-BRIEF-CARRIES-A-WALL-CLOCK-HOUR-COUNTER-SO-SESSION-BRIEF-GUARD-REDS-EVERY-REGISTER-TOUCHING-PR-ON-THE-CLOCK", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-THE-RENDERED-SESSION-BRIEF-CARRIES-A-WALL-CLOCK-HOUR-COUNTER-SO-SESSION-BRIEF-GUARD-REDS-EVERY-REGISTER-TOUCHING-PR-ON-THE-CLOCK", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-THE-RENDERED-SESSION-BRIEF-CARRIES-A-WALL-CLOCK-HOUR-COUNTER-SO-SESSION-BRIEF-GUARD-REDS-EVERY-REGISTER-TOUCHING-PR-ON-THE-CLOCK'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The generated CLAUDE.md SESSION-BRIEF embeds a wall-clock hour counter, so session-brief-guard re-reds any open register-touching PR as the clock ticks"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 45, "clears_when": "MECHANICALLY CHECKABLE, on purpose — a run of `check_register_ids.py --root <tmp> --base HEAD` over a register whose ONE shared id is wholesale-replaced (so R2a fires and `continue`s) must NOT print `R2b (replacement) 1/1 (100%)` for that register. It must report that 0 of 1 shared ids reached R2b, or name the short-circuited row, or otherwise distinguish 'not evaluated' from 'evaluated and clean'. ⚠️ A PASSING RUN CLEARS NOTHING: on a green run R2a never fires, every shared id does reach R2b, and 100% is the CORRECT reading — so the guard behaving on `main` is not evidence about this row and the check must be made against a deliberately R2a-failing tree. ⚠️ AND A TEST ASSERTING THE NEW STRING IS NOT SUFFICIENT ALONE without the positive control that a genuinely fully-evaluated register still reads 100%; deleting the number everywhere would pass a negative-only suite while destroying the census's ability to report full coverage — the exact trap #12398's own suite records hitting.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-REGISTER-ID-GUARD-PRINTS-R2B-COVERAGE-100-PERCENT-FOR-ROWS-R2A-SHORT-CIRCUITED-BEFORE-R2B-COULD-SEE-THEM", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-REGISTER-ID-GUARD-PRINTS-R2B-COVERAGE-100-PERCENT-FOR-ROWS-R2A-SHORT-CIRCUITED-BEFORE-R2B-COULD-SEE-THEM", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-REGISTER-ID-GUARD-PRINTS-R2B-COVERAGE-100-PERCENT-FOR-ROWS-R2A-SHORT-CIRCUITED-BEFORE-R2B-COULD-SEE-THEM'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] register-id-guard's census prints R2b coverage as 100% of shared ids, including rows R2a