{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, and they are different facts -- say WHICH was cleared. (1) A claude-pr-automerge run is OBSERVED printing a non-fallback opener with NO `could not construct a PAT-authenticated client` warning -- read off the run log, never from the workflow source. Alternatively the PAT branch is DELETED and that removal is recorded as a decision, which closes this row just as legitimately: a branch that never runs is worse than no branch, because a reader assumes it does. (2) The second observation is SETTLED with a positive control -- one bot-opened PR's check runs read at open time AND again after its first push, with both counts recorded, against the REQUIRED-check list read from branch protection. [!] A GREEN RUN OF claude-pr-automerge CLEARS NOTHING: every one of the five runs measured here concluded `success` while emitting the warning -- the fallback is silent by design and success is exactly what the broken state looks like. [!] AND THE SECRET BEING PRESENT CLEARS NOTHING EITHER: the failure is upstream of the token read.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-CLAUDE-PR-AUTOMERGE-CANNOT-CONSTRUCT-ITS-PAT-CLIENT-SO-THE-U2-PREVENTIONS-OPEN-UNDER-A-PAT-BRANCH-IS-INERT-IN-PRODUCTION", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-CLAUDE-PR-AUTOMERGE-CANNOT-CONSTRUCT-ITS-PAT-CLIENT-SO-THE-U2-PREVENTIONS-OPEN-UNDER-A-PAT-BRANCH-IS-INERT-IN-PRODUCTION", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-CLAUDE-PR-AUTOMERGE-CANNOT-CONSTRUCT-ITS-PAT-CLIENT-SO-THE-U2-PREVENTIONS-OPEN-UNDER-A-PAT-BRANCH-IS-INERT-IN-PRODUCTION'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] claude-pr-automerge falls back to GITHUB_TOKEN on every run because `@actions/github` is not resolvable from its script, so #11889's open-under-a-PAT branch has never run"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "A surviving fixture can no longer reach a commit -- demonstrated by planting the file, running `git add -A`, and observing it is NOT staged. [!] A CLEAN RUN CLOSES NOTHING: the fixture is removed correctly when the run completes, which is the state that already holds; the failure needs an INTERRUPTED run. [!] AND FIXING THE TWO DOWNSTREAM GUARDS TO IGNORE THE PATH IS THE WRONG REPAIR -- they reported truthfully about a file that was really in the diff.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-A-GUARD-SELF-TEST-PLANTS-A-SKILL-INTO-THE-WORKING-TREE-AND-A-BROAD-GIT-ADD-COMMITS-IT-WHICH-THEN-FAILS-TWO-OTHER-GUARDS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-A-GUARD-SELF-TEST-PLANTS-A-SKILL-INTO-THE-WORKING-TREE-AND-A-BROAD-GIT-ADD-COMMITS-IT-WHICH-THEN-FAILS-TWO-OTHER-GUARDS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-A-GUARD-SELF-TEST-PLANTS-A-SKILL-INTO-THE-WORKING-TREE-AND-A-BROAD-GIT-ADD-COMMITS-IT-WHICH-THEN-FAILS-TWO-OTHER-GUARDS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] guard_selftests.py plants .claude/skills/_selftest_doc_values/SKILL.md in the REAL tree; an interrupted run leaves it behind, `git add -A` commits it, and CI then fails document-index and skills-index on a skill nobody wrote"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, different facts -- say WHICH you cleared. (1) COVERAGE: a measured re-run of `open_pr_record.py --strict --open-prs <live list>` grades completeness=recorded, OR the operator decides the register is deliberately scoped to a subset and that decision is RECORDED -- in which case the file's own 'Every open PR must have a row' sentence must be corrected in the same change, because leaving it would keep this row true forever. A decision to scope it narrower is a legitimate outcome and clears this clause. (2) VISIBILITY: the completeness grade becomes reachable without a human remembering to pass --open-prs -- i.e. something that CAN fetch the live list (a workflow with a token, or the manager's check-in duty made explicit) runs it and the result lands where a successor reads it. !! CLEARING (1) WITHOUT (2) IS THE WEAKER HALF AND WILL SILENTLY ROT: rows written today decay as PRs open and merge, and nothing would report the decay -- which is how it reached 56. !! A GREEN `--strict` RUN CLEARS NOTHING: completeness is excluded from that exit code by design, so rc=0 is the state this row describes. !! AND A `not_observed` GRADE IS NOT A NEGATIVE -- it means nobody supplied live truth. Read the number, never the exit code.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-THE-OPEN-PR-HANDOFF-RECORD-COVERS-11-OF-67-OPEN-PRS-AND-ITS-COMPLETENESS-GRADE-IS-UNREACHABLE-FROM-CI", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-THE-OPEN-PR-HANDOFF-RECORD-COVERS-11-OF-67-OPEN-PRS-AND-ITS-COMPLETENESS-GRADE-IS-UNREACHABLE-FROM-CI", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-THE-OPEN-PR-HANDOFF-RECORD-COVERS-11-OF-67-OPEN-PRS-AND-ITS-COMPLETENESS-GRADE-IS-UNREACHABLE-FROM-CI'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] OPEN-PRS.json covers 11 of 67 open PRs, and the check that would say so cannot run where it matters"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "TWO PARTS, different facts -- say WHICH you cleared, and the SECOND is the one that matters. (1) THE RENDER STOPS LYING: a future-dated stamp is rendered DISTINGUISHABLY from a fresh one -- e.g. the age text reads `stamp is N min in the FUTURE` rather than `0.0h ago`. Demonstrate it with a positive control: show a future stamp and a just-made stamp producing DIFFERENT output, because today they produce identical output and that is the whole defect. (2) THE BAD VALUES ARE CORRECTED at source, and the writer that produced them is identified -- a bulk of 19 identical values is one event, so find it rather than hand-editing the rows. !! CORRECTING THE 20 STAMPS WITHOUT (1) CLEARS NOTHING AND IS THE WEAKER HALF: the clamp is still there and the next mistyped stamp reads as maximally fresh again. !! A GREEN TEST SUITE CLEARS NOTHING -- no test asserts on the future branch today, which is why it survived. !! AND DO NOT CLEAR THIS BY DELETING THE STAMPS: an absent `as_of` renders ', age unknown', which is honest and is a DIFFERENT state from both -- removing the field would hide the defect rather than fix it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-A-FUTURE-DATED-AS-OF-RENDERS-AS-JUST-OBSERVED-BECAUSE-THE-AGE-IS-CLAMPED-AT-ZERO", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-A-FUTURE-DATED-AS-OF-RENDERS-AS-JUST-OBSERVED-BECAUSE-THE-AGE-IS-CLAMPED-AT-ZERO", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-A-FUTURE-DATED-AS-OF-RENDERS-AS-JUST-OBSERVED-BECAUSE-THE-AGE-IS-CLAMPED-AT-ZERO'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A future-dated register stamp renders as '0.0h ago' — identical to one made this instant"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "EITHER runtime_logs/replay_pregate/** is added to TIER1_SURFACE in scripts/ci/check_pr_landing.py and a replay-pregate PR is OBSERVED passing pr-landing-guard, OR the generator declares `landing: hold` so the refusal is a deliberate human-read rather than an accident. !! A COMPLETED RUN DOES NOT CLEAR THIS and is the trap: the two blockers are independent, so a run that finally scores 22 heads would still be refused here. !! AND A GREEN `guards` ON SOME OTHER PR CLEARS NOTHING -- R5 keys on the PATH, so only a PR carrying a runtime_logs/ artifact exercises it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-PR-LANDING-R5-REFUSES-RUNTIME-LOGS-SO-REPLAY-PREGATE-CAN-NEVER-LAND-A-REPORT-EVEN-IF-IT-FINISHES", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-PR-LANDING-R5-REFUSES-RUNTIME-LOGS-SO-REPLAY-PREGATE-CAN-NEVER-LAND-A-REPORT-EVEN-IF-IT-FINISHES", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-PR-LANDING-R5-REFUSES-RUNTIME-LOGS-SO-REPLAY-PREGATE-CAN-NEVER-LAND-A-REPORT-EVEN-IF-IT-FINISHES'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] pr-landing R5 refuses runtime_logs/ so replay-pregate can never land a report, even if a run ever completes"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "A manager reads the 8 in_flight objects against live session state and moves each to its true lifecycle -- done/accepted where the owning session reported completed, or re-owned to a live session where the work genuinely continues. CLEARS when a later measurement of docs/claude/work/objects/ finds every in_flight object owned by a session whose get_session reports RUNNING, or explicitly owned by the manager with a stated reason.\n!! A COUNT BELOW 8 DOES NOT CLEAR THIS. The finding is that the in_flight set does not track liveness; a store at 5 in_flight with 5 dead owners is the same defect with more headroom.\n!! AND RAISING THE CEILING CLEARS NOTHING -- it would remove the symptom (a blocked lane) and leave the register just as wrong, which is worse because nothing would surface it again.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-THE-WIP-CEILING-IS-FULL-AND-SIX-OF-SIX-GRADEABLE-IN-FLIGHT-OWNERS-ARE-DEAD-SESSIONS-SO-A-NEW-LANE-CANNOT-RECORD-ITSELF", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-THE-WIP-CEILING-IS-FULL-AND-SIX-OF-SIX-GRADEABLE-IN-FLIGHT-OWNERS-ARE-DEAD-SESSIONS-SO-A-NEW-LANE-CANNOT-RECORD-ITSELF", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-THE-WIP-CEILING-IS-FULL-AND-SIX-OF-SIX-GRADEABLE-IN-FLIGHT-OWNERS-ARE-DEAD-SESSIONS-SO-A-NEW-LANE-CANNOT-RECORD-ITSELF'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] The WIP ceiling is at 8/8 and six of six gradeable in-flight owners are dead sessions, so a newly-spawned lane cannot record itself in_flight"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "EITHER (a) /api/diag/journal honours offset= and a probe demonstrates it — limit=1000&offset=1000 returns an id range DISJOINT from limit=1000&offset=0, verified by comparing the two id SETS rather than by reading the diff; OR (b) the route REFUSES an unsupported parameter with a 4xx naming it, so a caller learns immediately. A DOC NOTE ALONE DOES NOT CLOSE THIS: the /api/bot/performance days= precedent is already documented in CLAUDE.md and was still hit by a session on this same day, because the surface that lies is the one a caller reads, not the doc. AND A GREEN TEST CLEARS NOTHING: the defect is in what the LIVE route does with an extra query parameter; a harness asserting the cap does not exercise it.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-THE-DIAG-JOURNAL-OFFSET-PARAMETER-IS-SILENTLY-IGNORED-SO-A-SESSION-PAGING-FOR-A-WIDER-CORPUS-GETS-THE-SAME-1000-ROWS-EVERY-TIME", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-THE-DIAG-JOURNAL-OFFSET-PARAMETER-IS-SILENTLY-IGNORED-SO-A-SESSION-PAGING-FOR-A-WIDER-CORPUS-GETS-THE-SAME-1000-ROWS-EVERY-TIME", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-THE-DIAG-JOURNAL-OFFSET-PARAMETER-IS-SILENTLY-IGNORED-SO-A-SESSION-PAGING-FOR-A-WIDER-CORPUS-GETS-THE-SAME-1000-ROWS-EVERY-TIME'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] /api/diag/journal accepts offset= and IGNORES it — limit=1000&offset=1000 returns the IDENTICAL id range (4882,5881) as offset=0 with no error, so a session paging for a wider corpus gets the same 1000 rows every time and believes it has N x 1000"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 14, "clears_when": "THE RULE MUST BE CARRIED BY SOMETHING A MANAGER MEETS BEFORE IT DISPATCHES, not by another memo. Clears when BOTH: (a) the spawn-vs-resume test is written into CLAUDE.md's manager section AND docs/claude/work/README.md -- REUSE only when the next unit's inputs live in that session's context AND are not readable from the repo or a named branch; otherwise SPAWN FRESH -- with the measured basis above beside it so it cannot be read as a preference; and (b) a manager is OBSERVED choosing fresh on a unit it would previously have resumed, and saying WHICH limb of the test decided it. [!] (a) ALONE DOES NOT CLEAR IT. This repo's own record is that a reminder is not a mechanism -- the manager-scope rule needed a CI check after a fourth restatement failed. If (b) does not follow, the honest next step is a CHECK (e.g. requiring a resume to record its stated context-dependency, so a resume with none is visible), not a fifth paragraph. [!] DO NOT CLEAR THIS BY BANNING RESUME. Resume is CORRECT when the context is genuinely unrepeatable -- an investigation mid-flight, a measurement whose intermediate state was never landed -- and a blanket ban would force lanes to rebuild state the repo does not hold, which is the opposite waste. [!] AND A QUIET MONTH IS NOT EVIDENCE: the cost is silent by construction, so 'nobody complained' cannot distinguish the rule being followed from the rule being unknown. Read the cache_read delta on a resumed lane before reading any quiet as a pass.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-A-LANE-IS-RESUMED-BY-DEFAULT-SO-A-FRESH-UNIT-PAYS-THE-PREDECESSORS-WHOLE-CONTEXT-AS-CACHE-READS-EVERY-TURN", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-A-LANE-IS-RESUMED-BY-DEFAULT-SO-A-FRESH-UNIT-PAYS-THE-PREDECESSORS-WHOLE-CONTEXT-AS-CACHE-READS-EVERY-TURN", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-A-LANE-IS-RESUMED-BY-DEFAULT-SO-A-FRESH-UNIT-PAYS-THE-PREDECESSORS-WHOLE-CONTEXT-AS-CACHE-READS-EVERY-TURN'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] A spawned lane is resumed by default, not started fresh — so a unit that doesn't need the predecessor's context still pays the whole thing back as cache-read tokens every turn"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 30, "clears_when": "BOTH, and they are different facts. (1) The model-to-task rule is written where a manager reads it BEFORE spawning — CLAUDE.md's manager section and docs/claude/work/README.md — naming the model ids and stating that the default is INHERITANCE, so choosing is an ACT. That is carried by WO-20260917-CANONIZE-SPAWN-VS-RESUME-AND-MODEL-TO-TASK. (2) A manager is OBSERVED passing an explicit `model` on a spawn and recording WHY that model fits that unit — in the SESSIONS.json row, so a successor can read the reasoning and not just the value. [!] A CANON EDIT ALONE DOES NOT CLOSE THIS: prose-only has already failed twice on the manager's own duties (MI-15 twice, BL-20260903-MANAGER-CHECKLIST-GOES-STALE-SILENTLY-AND-STATUS-REPORTS-IT-AS-CURRENT), which is why clause (2) asks for an observation and not a document. [!] AND A SPAWN-TIME CHECK IS NOT ASKED FOR AND MUST NOT BE INVENTED TO CLOSE THIS: CI cannot read a create_session call, so a guard here would grade the RECORD of a choice rather than the choice — the shape CLAUDE.md already refuses for operator feedback. If someone builds one anyway, it is a separate proposal with its own row.", "kind": "observation", "last_checked": "2026-09-21"}, "id": "BL-20260917-A-SPAWNED-LANE-INHERITS-THE-MANAGERS-MODEL-SO-EVERY-LANE-RUNS-ON-OPUS-WITHOUT-ANYONE-CHOOSING-IT", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260917-A-SPAWNED-LANE-INHERITS-THE-MANAGERS-MODEL-SO-EVERY-LANE-RUNS-ON-OPUS-WITHOUT-ANYONE-CHOOSING-IT", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260917-A-SPAWNED-LANE-INHERITS-THE-MANAGERS-MODEL-SO-EVERY-LANE-RUNS-ON-OPUS-WITHOUT-ANYONE-CHOOSING-IT'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "[health] create_session's model parameter defaults to the CALLING session's model, so a manager that spawns without passing model gives every lane its own model by accident -- measured both live lanes on 2026-09-17 running claude-opus-5 with no model argument passed"}
