{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260907-TRAINER-DIAG-RELAY-DISCARDS-A-COMPUTED-RESULT-ON-A-PUSH-RACE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260907-TRAINER-DIAG-RELAY-DISCARDS-A-COMPUTED-RESULT-ON-A-PUSH-RACE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260907-TRAINER-DIAG-RELAY-DISCARDS-A-COMPUTED-RESULT-ON-A-PUSH-RACE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "trainer-diag-relay.yml's commit-back step is `git push origin HEAD:${{ github.ref_name }}` under `set -euo pipefail`, with no rebase and no retry. When a second relay triggered by the SAME push (board-post.yml, pr-opener.yml) commits to the branch first, the relay's push is a non-fast-forward, the step fails, and a result it had ALREADY COMPUTED on the trainer is discarded. Measured 2026-09-07 (MI-154b): request mi154b-scalp-probe-20260907 produced no result after a push that also carried automation/board-posts/; board-post committed 228f2719 first and the relay lost the race. Re-sent ALONE under a fresh name, the identical script returned state=ran remote_exit=0 in ~30s. WHY IT IS WORSE THAN A LOST RUN: the failure presents as an ABSENT result file, byte-identical to 'the relay never fired' and to 'the trainer is unreachable' -- three faults with three different remedies collapsed into one silent state, and the natural first suspicion is the trainer's health, which was fine throughout. It cost ~25 minutes of misdiagnosis. All three push-triggered relays (trainer-diag-relay, board-post, pr-opener) share this commit-back shape, so any two triggered by one push can collide."}
