{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-STRATEGY-REVIEW-PACKET-GRADES-EDGE-OFF-A-LIVE-WINDOW-WHICH-THE-PROMOTION-EVIDENCE-RULE-FORBIDS", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-STRATEGY-REVIEW-PACKET-GRADES-EDGE-OFF-A-LIVE-WINDOW-WHICH-THE-PROMOTION-EVIDENCE-RULE-FORBIDS", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-STRATEGY-REVIEW-PACKET-GRADES-EDGE-OFF-A-LIVE-WINDOW-WHICH-THE-PROMOTION-EVIDENCE-RULE-FORBIDS'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "The M7 strategy-review packet withholds every verdict for want of LIVE in-window closes (MIN_CLOSED_FOR_ACTION = 20 over a 7-day window), which is a CALENDAR-ACCRUAL GATE FOR EDGE. docs/CLAUDE-RULES-CANONICAL.md 'Promotion evidence - offline edge, live mechanics' has been BINDING since 2026-07-26 and its clause 3 forbids exactly that: 'No gate may require calendar-time accrual to prove edge.' Its scope is explicitly STRATEGY legs, not only ML heads, and it names this failure as 'the recurring drift this rule kills'. MEASURED 2026-09-09 over all 8 committed daily indexes (2026-09-01..09-08), all 52 enabled legs: graded 52 / actionable 0 / by_action {hold: 52} on 8 of 8 days; no leg reached 11 closes in a 7-day window on any day; 29-32 of 52 sit at zero every day. OPERATOR VERDICT 2026-09-09: the question of how to set window/floor is VOID - 'we do NOT rely on live soaking for validating strategies, only mechanics', and slow live accrual is 'a feature of the system', not a barrier. THE FIX IS NOT A TUNING: the packet must take its edge verdict from the OFFLINE backtest evidence the repo already has (purged walk-forward oos_edge, replay_pregate_fleet, the backfills) and use live rows only for MECHANICS. Do NOT lower the floor and do NOT widen the window - both keep the prohibited instrument and merely re-scale it. Entry points: scripts/ml/strategy_review_packet.py (MIN_CLOSED_FOR_ACTION), src/runtime/evidence_horizon.py, scripts/ml/evidence_floor_report.py. Tier-3 where it changes what a KILL/DEMOTE verdict rests on - propose, do not enact."}
{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-THE-MANAGER-SCOPE-CARVE-OUT-ADMITS-A-MERGE-SLOT-CLAIM-BUT-CANNOT-EXPRESS-A-RELEASE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-THE-MANAGER-SCOPE-CARVE-OUT-ADMITS-A-MERGE-SLOT-CLAIM-BUT-CANNOT-EXPRESS-A-RELEASE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-THE-MANAGER-SCOPE-CARVE-OUT-ADMITS-A-MERGE-SLOT-CLAIM-BUT-CANNOT-EXPRESS-A-RELEASE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "check_manager_scope.py R2 admits a manager commit to docs/claude/session-board.json for EXACTLY one thing: a `merge_slot` claim naming the branch being landed. It cannot express a RELEASE (held_by -> null). OBSERVED 2026-09-09: the manager wrote a release after #11524 merged and R2 refused it with 'merge_slot.branch is None, not this branch'. So a manager who has finished landing has only two moves, and both are bad: leave a STALE claim naming a merged branch, or violate R2. THE STALE-CLAIM BRANCH IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL AND IT HAS A MEASURED COST: earlier the same day the slot sat held for claude/mgr-dispatch-lane2-refill-20260909 for ~25 minutes after its PR #11511 had merged, and lane 2 had to announce and DISPLACE it before it could land #11514. That lane handled it correctly, which is the point - the cost landed on someone else. ⚠️ THIS IS A GAP IN THE CARVE-OUT, NOT AN ARGUMENT TO WIDEN R2. Releasing is a LANDING act by exactly the same reasoning that admits the claim, so the narrow fix is to admit a transition to a null/released slot BY THE SESSION THAT HOLDS IT - never a general permission to write session-board.json, which would re-open the hole the carve-out exists to close. ⚠️ AND NOTE THE MITIGATION THAT ALREADY EXISTS, so this is not urgent: R13 does not serialize (its own docstring says so) and slots are displaced freely, so a stale claim delays rather than blocks. Entry point: scripts/ci/check_manager_scope.py R2, the merge_slot carve-out."}
{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-GUARDS-ARE-BEING-WRITTEN-AS-BANS-ON-ASKING-A-QUESTION-WHICH-SUPPRESSES-THE-SYMPTOM-AND-LEAVES-THE-MISUNDERSTANDING", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-GUARDS-ARE-BEING-WRITTEN-AS-BANS-ON-ASKING-A-QUESTION-WHICH-SUPPRESSES-THE-SYMPTOM-AND-LEAVES-THE-MISUNDERSTANDING", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-GUARDS-ARE-BEING-WRITTEN-AS-BANS-ON-ASKING-A-QUESTION-WHICH-SUPPRESSES-THE-SYMPTOM-AND-LEAVES-THE-MISUNDERSTANDING'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "OPERATOR-RAISED 2026-09-09, verbatim: \"you keep adding guards in the shape of forbidding questions from being asked - this is incorrect. the problem isn't the question, it's the underlying misunderstanding of infra and processes, and not asking questions isn't what fixes that - it just makes it more likely that you will f****** again in the future because you're not asking the right question. so when I'm upset about isn't that you're asking the same question over and over again. it's that you don't understand how the system works. that's what we need to fix here, not the question\". INSTANCE: the manager's MI-215 dispatch brief and checklist note read 'DO NOT RE-ASK THE WINDOW/FLOOR QUESTION IN ANY FORM'. The same session had, hours earlier, put a four-option decision to the operator in which ALL FOUR options rested on a false model of how this system establishes evidence — and then 'prevented' the recurrence by banning the question rather than by conveying the model. WHY IT IS WORSE THAN A NO-OP: a question-ban removes the one signal that a session does not understand something, so the misunderstanding survives and surfaces later as a DIFFERENT wrong action that nobody saw coming. It also trains sessions not to surface the very confusions the operator most wants surfaced. THE CORRECT SHAPES, all of which this repo already uses elsewhere: (a) enforce the RULE the misunderstanding violates (here: a gate producing a STRATEGY verdict must source edge from offline evidence) rather than a phrase; (b) make the SURFACE state the basis of its own output, the diagnostic-provenance discipline; (c) put the MODEL in the brief so a session can reason from it and disagree with it. ⚠️ NOTE THE LEGITIMATE NEIGHBOUR AND DO NOT OVER-CORRECT INTO IT: constraining an ACTION with its reason stated ('propose, never enact'; 'do not restore the pre-2026-08-14 flat bail, because the static DD floor binds while flat') is NOT this defect — it is a tier rule or a stated hazard, and it explains itself. The defect is specifically forbidding an INQUIRY."}
{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-WHERE-ELSE-DOES-THE-OPERATING-LAYER-ASSUME-LIVE-ACCRUAL-PROVES-EDGE-NOBODY-HAS-COUNTED", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-WHERE-ELSE-DOES-THE-OPERATING-LAYER-ASSUME-LIVE-ACCRUAL-PROVES-EDGE-NOBODY-HAS-COUNTED", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-WHERE-ELSE-DOES-THE-OPERATING-LAYER-ASSUME-LIVE-ACCRUAL-PROVES-EDGE-NOBODY-HAS-COUNTED'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "OPERATOR-RAISED 2026-09-09: \"our overall operation is clearly not built to suit the system's structure\". The system establishes EDGE offline (the backtesting infrastructure) and uses live data for MECHANICS. The operating layer around it repeatedly assumes the opposite — that live outcomes accrue until a verdict becomes possible. The M7 strategy-review packet is ONE confirmed instance (MI-215): it withholds all 52 verdicts for want of live in-window closes. ⚠️ THE POINT OF THIS ROW IS THAT NOBODY HAS COUNTED THE OTHERS, and one instance is not a population. Candidate surfaces to CHECK, not to assume: promotion/demotion gates, the soak framing throughout OPEN-ITEMS.json clears_when texts, `days_to_grade` style horizon reporting, the review skills' own rubrics, `snoozed_until` accrual rows in the backlogs, and any `MIN_*` / `*_MIN_N` constant applied to a LIVE window. For each: does it decide EDGE or MECHANICS, and does it require calendar time to reach a verdict? ⚠️ STATE THE POPULATION AND CARRY A POSITIVE CONTROL — a probe that finds nothing must be shown able to find the known instance (the M7 packet) first, or its silence means nothing. ⚠️ THIS IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A LICENCE TO CHANGE GATES. Report the count and the list; each fix is its own scoped decision, and anything touching what a promotion or KILL rests on is Tier-3. ⚠️ FILING NOTE: an earlier wording of this row's exit condition tripped `accrual-clock guard`, which matches the word 'accrual' and demanded an `accrual_legs` list. That was a FALSE POSITIVE of the narrow kind that module's own comment says it wants to avoid — this row waits on a COUNT, not on trades — and it is a hazard specific to a row whose SUBJECT is calendar-accrual assumptions. Resolved the way the guard itself prescribes, by re-stating the exit condition as the measurement it really is, NOT by adding a fake leg list or weakening the guard. Recorded here so the next author of such a row does not read the failure as their row being wrong."}
{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-PR-LANDING-HOLD-REASONS-HAS-NO-VALUE-FOR-TIER-1-ON-AN-UNCERTIFIABLE-PATH", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-PR-LANDING-HOLD-REASONS-HAS-NO-VALUE-FOR-TIER-1-ON-AN-UNCERTIFIABLE-PATH", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-PR-LANDING-HOLD-REASONS-HAS-NO-VALUE-FOR-TIER-1-ON-AN-UNCERTIFIABLE-PATH'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "scripts/ci/check_pr_landing.py::HOLD_REASONS is a closed set of five, and none of them expresses the case R5 itself produces most often for a Tier-1 PR: work that IS Tier-1 by docs/CLAUDE-RULES-CANONICAL.md § Permission Tiers ('Docs, tests, CI, tooling') but touches a path TIER1_SURFACE does not enumerate, so the guard declines to CERTIFY it and directs the author to `landing: \"hold\"`. Hit 2026-09-09 by MI-215 (PR #11529) on scripts/check_soak_doctrine.py: TIER1_SURFACE lists scripts/ci/**, scripts/ops/**, scripts/research/** and scripts/reports/**, but NOT the scripts/ root, where check_soak_doctrine.py, check_provenance_consumers.py and check_diagnostic_provenance.py all live. The author must then pick `tier_2_3_needs_approval`, whose own description reads 'Tier-2/Tier-3 work' -- so the typed reason contradicts the `tier: 1` field two lines above it. ⚠️ THE HARM IS TO THE TYPED VOCABULARY, NOT TO THIS PR. R7's docstring says the closed set exists so 'a hold is a stated KIND of hold and not an adjective', mirroring the operator_decision discipline in OPEN-PRS.json. A token routinely used to mean something other than what it says is exactly the drift that discipline prevents, and it degrades quietly: every such PR reads afterwards as Tier-2/3 work awaiting approval when it was Tier-1 awaiting a certification the guard could not give."}
