S-2026-09-09.md."}
{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-DEFAULT-PROMOTION-PROFILE-REQUIRES-A-7-DAY-CALENDAR-SOAK-AND-200-LIVE-TRADES", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-DEFAULT-PROMOTION-PROFILE-REQUIRES-A-7-DAY-CALENDAR-SOAK-AND-200-LIVE-TRADES", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-DEFAULT-PROMOTION-PROFILE-REQUIRES-A-7-DAY-CALENDAR-SOAK-AND-200-LIVE-TRADES'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "MI-218 CONFIRMED SURFACE S2, and the highest-leverage one found. ml/promotion/gates.py:228 picks `regime_classifier_thresholds()` if `is_regime_classifier(entry)` else a bare `GateThresholds()`. The regime profile sets `require_shadow_soak=False` (WS-1 de-soak, operator-approved 2026-07-26) and `min_trades=5`. EVERY OTHER HEAD lands on the default, where BOTH are REQUIRED: `require_shadow_soak=True` @ `shadow_soak_days=7.0` — a literal 'N days at stage', which CLAUDE-RULES-CANONICAL.md § 'Promotion evidence' clause 3 names verbatim as 'a policy artifact, not evidence' — and `min_trades=200` LIVE trades, which at the ~1.2 closes/week the operator cites is ~3.2 YEARS. ⚠️ CANON SAYS THIS IS 'mechanically guarded: tests/ml/test_gates.py asserts that no required gate UNDER THE REGIME-CLASSIFIER PROFILE is a calendar-time edge gate'. That is TRUE and it is SCOPED TO ONE PROFILE. The default profile — used by every non-regime head, including trade-outcome and exit heads — is not covered by that assertion. This is the M7 fact pattern one level up: the rule is binding, the guard is real, and the guard does not reach the surface. Evidence: docs/research/CALENDAR-TIME-EDGE-SURFACE-CENSUS-2026-09-09.md § S2."}
{"due_when": {"due_date": "2026-09-21", "kind": "date"}, "id": "BL-20260909-BACKTEST-FIDELITY-MAKES-30-LIVE-TRADES-A-PRECONDITION-FOR-TRUSTING-OFFLINE-EDGE", "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "review", "ref": "docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json#BL-20260909-BACKTEST-FIDELITY-MAKES-30-LIVE-TRADES-A-PRECONDITION-FOR-TRUSTING-OFFLINE-EDGE", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/registers/health-review-backlog.json')); items=d['items'] if isinstance(d, dict) else d; print(json.dumps(next(i for i in items if i.get('id')=='BL-20260909-BACKTEST-FIDELITY-MAKES-30-LIVE-TRADES-A-PRECONDITION-FOR-TRUSTING-OFFLINE-EDGE'), indent=2))\""}, "state": "killed", "terminal_reason": "unworked_since_never", "what": "MI-218 CONFIRMED SURFACE S3, and the sharpest instance of the doctrine inverted. scripts/research/backtest_fidelity_calibrate.py::agreement holds `MIN_LIVE_N = 30`; below it the verdict is `insufficient-live` and, in the script's own words, 'backtest is a lead, not a result'. Its OWN docstring states the problem it was built to solve: 'we have never MEASURED whether our backtests are right, so we fell back to only trust real live trades — WHICH CAPS EVERY DECISION AT REALITY'S CLOCK'. The implementation then makes 30 LIVE trades a precondition for a leg's OFFLINE evidence being admissible — ~25 weeks at ~1.2 closes/week. So the instrument built to escape reality's clock is reachable only by waiting on it. ⚠️ STATED FAIRLY, THIS IS NOT A SIMPLE DEFECT: measuring backtest<->live fidelity DOES require live trades, and abstaining is honest rather than a silent pass. The finding is narrower and is the part that contradicts canon: a FIDELITY (mechanics) measurement is used as the ADMISSIBILITY GATE ON AN EDGE CLAIM, so a leg with a clean purged-WF-CV oos_edge and 29 live trades has evidence the system will not look at. Evidence: docs/research/CALENDAR-TIME-EDGE-SURFACE-CENSUS-2026-09-09.md § S3."}
