{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "The Workflow page either lists the operator decisions that actually exist (the checklist's recorded answers and the pipeline's ask_operator rows), or states that its source is unreadable — and in NO case renders 'Nothing is waiting on you' when it has not looked. Verified by the OPERATOR loading the page and seeing a true count, not by reading the diff.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-M09", "loud": true, "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "operator", "ref": "operator screenshot of the live Workflow page, 2026-09-21 22:35 local; confirmed against src/web/api/routers/work.py::_decision_inbox and the absent docs/claude/work/objects/", "rerun": "ls -d docs/claude/work/objects 2>&1; grep -n '_objects_dir\\|decision_requests' src/web/api/routers/work.py | head; # FINDING STILL APPLIES while the directory is absent AND _decision_inbox still sources from it"}, "state": "queued", "what": "THE 'WAITING ON YOU' PANEL IS A FALSE ALL-CLEAR, ON THE OPERATOR'S OWN PAGE. It renders 'Nothing is waiting on you right now. 0 answered decision(s) are on record — 0 through this channel, 0 in conversation.' MEASURED 2026-09-21: src/web/api/routers/work.py::_decision_inbox sources its questions from docs/claude/work/objects/*.yaml :: decision_requests[], and THAT DIRECTORY WAS ARCHIVED BY THE 2026-09-21 RESET (it now lives at docs/archive/2026-09-21-operating-reset/work/objects). _yaml_files() returns [] for an absent directory, so the panel is describing an empty folder, not reality. [!] THE OPERATOR ANSWERED FIVE DECISIONS TODAY and the page says zero are on record: the spawn-provenance grant, the settings.json grant, R6 (keep the roster, decide after D1/R1), B1's four-clause evidence bar with the minimum-n clause declined, and B2 (strict equality). All five are recorded in MANAGER-CHECKLIST.json `note` fields, which this panel does not read. [!] THE SERIOUS HALF IS NOT THE MISSING HISTORY, IT IS THE ALL-CLEAR. A genuine unanswered operator decision would render IDENTICALLY to none existing, because 'we could not look' and 'there is nothing' are collapsed — the exact class scripts/ci/check_collapsed_states.py enforces against, on the one page built so work is not dropped. It is the same reader-orphan pattern E9 fixed for the coverage, sessions and WIP panels and did not reach. [!] DO NOT fix it by resurrecting the work store. Decisions now live on the checklist and in the pipeline (next_action: ask_operator); either the panel reads those, or it says plainly that it cannot read its source — never 'nothing is waiting on you'."}
