o prop trade notification in a suspiciously long time. MEASURED the same hour off the live host: newest account_status is 2026-08-30T19:33:29Z (528.4h, `stale` against a 24h gate), newest ticket 2026-09-13 `expired`, no fill since 2026-08-30, distance_to_daily_loss_usd null. So the predicted state is the observed state and the discovery method was a human noticing an ABSENCE -- not the alert this row asks for. [!] THE ROW IS NOT CLEARED BY THAT. Its clears_when demands the refusal message reaching an operator-facing channel, read off a live surface; a human independently noticing the silence is the failure it describes, not the fix. [!] AND THE OPERATOR'S OTHER DECISION THE SAME DAY RAISES THE STAKES: the periodic status ask now fires only on new exposure, so the one thing that WAS noisy in the stalled state is going away. E16 is instructed not to ship that silencing without the refusal signal in the same landing. [!] UPDATED 2026-09-21 AFTER E16 LANDED (#12696, merged 635600c): the refusal now pages the operator through the pending_pings inbox, keyed on the STATE rather than the message (the `stale` reason embeds the snapshot's age, so a naive 'page when the reason changes' rule would fire once per tick -- pinned by test_a_stale_refusal_pages_once_not_once_per_tick). ⚠️ THIS ROW IS MOVED, NOT CLOSED, and the lane said so itself rather than claiming the close. Its clears_when states the gap is WHICH CHANNEL the message reaches and that a passing test does not close it. What is established is MERGED. ⚠️ AND THE OBSERVATION IS CURRENTLY UNMAKEABLE: it needs a prop_sizing_refusal row read off the live host, and the vm-diag-snapshot relay is failing (row E19). ⚠️ NOTE THE LIMIT OF WHAT THIS FIXES: the three-week silence produced NO refusal at all -- breakout_1 was never reached, not blocked -- so this ping would not have caught it. That detector is row E18.", "state": "routed", "what": "[health] A prop account blocked from trading by a stale balance stops trading with NO operator-facing signal — the refusal is journaled and logged, and the ping that exists for exactly this is on a different branch"}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 21, "clears_when": "`--population` reports passing == roster_slots, OR the operator rules per leg on the grandfathered twelve. A partial improvement is NOT a clear: the number that matters is how many real-money legs still trade on evidence that does not meet the bar, and that is only zero at zero.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-0011", "loud": true, "next_action": "check_observation", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "session_01K4v2zisKhUyNaXsm2cSmgg (B1 build lane, 2026-09-21) -- PR #12688, commit 520a69d56", "rerun": "python3 scripts/ci/check_roster_promotion_evidence.py --population   # FINDING STILL APPLIES while the 'clear the four-clause bar' line reads less than the 'roster slots' line. Use --json for the per-leg failed-clause list."}, "routed_to": "Blocked on D1 (cost stack in the harnesses / the evidence producer) and B5 (the pre-registration mechanism). Neither is this lane's; both are existing checklist rows. When either lands, re-run the census and route the remainder to the operator per leg -- a leg that cannot be evidenced is a DEMOTION candidate, and demotion needs nothing.", "state": "queued", "what": "TWELVE LEGS SIT ON A RISK-BEARING ROSTER AND ZERO CARRY AN EVIDENCE RECORD THAT CLEARS THE OPERATOR'S FOUR-CLAUSE BAR. MEASURED 2026-09-21 by `python3 scripts/ci/check_roster_promotion_evidence.py --population` on commit 520a69d56. Population: every leg in `strategies:` on an account whose config/accounts.yaml account_class is not `paper` -- alpaca_live (3), breakout_1 (3, class `prop`), bybit_2 (6), ib_live (0) = 12 roster slots, 12 distinct legs. Graded against comms/strategy_evidence/<leg>.json: 0 pass, 12 fail. [!] ELEVEN OF TWELVE FAIL EXACTLY C3 AND C4, and both are corpus-wide rather than leg-specific. C3 (net of the FULL cost stack): no record carries slippage or funding at all; across all 52 committed records the only cost field is fee_bps_roundtrip in {0.0, 7.5, None}. That is the fee-only corpus CLAUDE.md already names as the reason the real-money promotion mandate does not arm until D1. C4 (a rule registered BEFORE the run): param_selection_provenance reads `not_established` on 52 of 52 records; no record has ever claimed a pre-registered rule. C1/C2 additionally fail for bybit_2/fvg_range_15m, whose coverage_state is `no_harness` -- per the comms/strategy_evidence README that is a statement about US, not about the strategy. [!] THIS DEBT IS GRANDFATHERED ON PURPOSE. roster-promotion-evidence-guard (PR #12688) is DIFF-SCOPED, so it blocks the thirteenth leg and says nothing about these twelve; a whole-tree version would red every PR in the repo over legs nobody is proposing to promote. The twelve are therefore invisible to CI by design and will stay invisible unless something re-asks. This row is that something. [!] IT IS NOT ACTIONABLE YET AND THAT IS THE POINT: no producer writes a cost_stack block (D1) and no mechanism registers a rule before a run (B5), so re-running the census today can only return 0/12 again. Re-ask when D1 or B5 lands."}
