{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "Either a lane is observed completing a commit+push having been dispatched with the mitigation in place AND the refused shape is named from evidence rather than inferred, or the permission configuration is changed so the prompt cannot arise unattended. ⚠️ A lane that happens to succeed proves nothing on its own -- lanes succeeded all day while this was happening; the clearing evidence must name what was refused.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-LANE-BLOCKED-ON-AN-UNATTENDED-PERMISSION-PROMPT", "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "Manager session_01XQhayAHWdrSYv8jN54P2HH, 2026-09-21. Read from get_session on session_011b88KXF5rUPYPbUWARAtEy (status_detail: '4 edits staged; git commit denied by permission rule') and session_018J9SUp957b1V5xj1mcfTWu (pending_action, raw_command quoted above).", "rerun": "Call get_session on a lane that reports status_bucket SESSION_STATUS_BUCKET_BLOCKED and read external_metadata.pending_action.raw_command."}, "routed_to": "Checklist row E20, cause (3). ⚠️ THE COMMAND-SHAPE EXPLANATION IS A HYPOTHESIS AND MUST BE TESTED BEFORE IT BECOMES A DISPATCH RULE: other lanes committed and pushed all day, so whatever is refused is not universal. Establish which shapes are refused, with a positive control that shows the probe can see an ALLOWED command too -- a rule written from a guess is the category of error this repo keeps paying for.", "state": "routed", "what": "A dispatched lane can stop on an interactive Bash permission prompt in a session nobody is watching, and spend its entire budget there. MEASURED 2026-09-21 on checklist row B2: the first lane reached $229.13 against a $30 ceiling and committed nothing, ending on 'git commit denied by permission rule'; the re-dispatch stalled at the same wall with its pending action readable as a COMPOUND, PIPED git command (`git fetch origin main 2>&1 | tail -5 && git merge origin/main --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -60`).", "why_it_matters": "It converts a four-line, fully-specified, operator-approved config edit into two dead lanes and $229, and it is silent: the lane reports `need_input` to a parent that is not watching for it, so the money is spent before anyone knows there is a question. It also means a lane's ceiling does not bound the damage, because the spend is not going into work."}
