e` account and the deleted fallback covered 0 of them. [!] WHAT IS NOT YET ESTABLISHED, and is the whole point of this row: the live trader is a long-running process whose `STRATEGIES` is evaluated ONCE at import, so NONE of this reaches production until ict-trader-live is RESTARTED after the deploy. ict-git-sync pulls main every ~5 min but does not restart the trader. So `merged` will be true and `deployed` false for an unbounded window, and `observed` needs a third fact on top of that. [!] CORRECTION, 2026-09-22, same session, BEFORE this row was acted on: the sentence above saying ict-git-sync 'does not restart the trader' is WRONG and is withdrawn. VERIFIED by reading deploy/ict-git-sync.service (ExecStart=bash scripts/deploy_pull_restart.sh) and scripts/deploy_pull_restart.sh: the deploy DOES `systemctl restart ict-trader-live ict-telegram-bot ict-web-api`, driven off runtime_logs/deployed_sha.txt rather than off whether this fetch moved HEAD, and it SKIPS the restart only when every changed path is non-runtime (docs/, tests/, .claude/, .github/, top-level *.md). This diff touches src/, so the restart fires. WHAT THAT CHANGES: `deployed` follows `merged` automatically within about one 5-minute timer tick instead of waiting on a manual restart. WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE: `observed` is still a separate fact and still needs the two reads in clears_when -- a restart having been ISSUED is not the same as the new check appearing in a snapshot.", "why_it_matters": "The defect being fixed is an exit-path outage on a live real-money system that presents as `7/7 checks ok`. A fix for a silent failure that is itself unobserved reproduces the same condition one level up -- this repo's most-paid-for mistake is collapsing merged / deployed / observed."}
