{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 21, "clears_when": "m20-exit-lever-sweep.yml and research-exit-head-build.yml declare research_unit (and power_state) as workflow_dispatch inputs and stamp them onto the rows they land, as e35-bracket-sweep.yml does -- at which point RQ-20260922-003/004/007 flip to queued.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260922-RESEARCH-UNIT-STAMP-ONLY-ON-E35", "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "checklist C5/R4 research lane, session_01AHNgatHswZsemNiP8aSXCk, branch claude/c5-r4-ten-research-questions", "rerun": "python3 -c \"import yaml,glob;\\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('.github/workflows/*.yml')):\\n d=yaml.safe_load(open(f)) or {};\\n on=d.get(True) or d.get('on') or {};\\n ins=((on.get('workflow_dispatch') or {}).get('inputs') or {});\\n print(f, 'research_unit' in ins, 'power_state' in ins)\""}, "state": "queued", "what": "dispatch_queue.py REFUSES to fire an `accruing` or `underpowered` unit unless it declares run.inputs.research_unit, so the power verdict is stamped onto the rows the run lands. MEASURED 2026-09-22 by reading the workflow_dispatch inputs of e35-bracket-sweep.yml, m20-exit-lever-sweep.yml, pullback-frac-cross-leg-sweep.yml, research-exit-head-build.yml and regime-debt-matrix.yml: ONLY e35-bracket-sweep.yml declares research_unit (and power_state). The dispatcher's own note says `gh workflow run -f <undeclared-input>` ERRORS, so declaring it anyway fails at fire time while omitting it is refused at grade time. Net effect: an honestly-declared accruing unit can route to exactly ONE of the repo's ~20 research workflows. This is why RQ-20260922-003, -004 and -007 ship `blocked` rather than `queued`."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 21, "clears_when": "dispatch_queue.py short-circuits on status before schema validation, or emits a distinct outcome (e.g. `blocked`) for a unit whose status is blocked, so `deliberately parked` and `malformed` are distinguishable in the census.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260922-DISPATCHER-REPORTS-A-BLOCKED-UNIT-AS-INVALID", "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "checklist C5/R4 research lane, session_01AHNgatHswZsemNiP8aSXCk, branch claude/c5-r4-ten-research-questions", "rerun": "python3 scripts/research/dispatch_queue.py   # compare the outcome column against each unit's `status:` field"}, "state": "queued", "what": "dispatch_queue.py validates run.workflow BEFORE it reads status, so a unit that is DELIBERATELY blocked with run.workflow: null reports `invalid -- run.workflow is required`, identically to a malformed job. OBSERVED 2026-09-22 on this branch: RQ-20260922-001/002/006/010 are all status: blocked with a named blocker and all four print `invalid`, while RQ-20260922-003/004/007 (blocked, but carrying a workflow) correctly print `not_due status=blocked`. Two states sharing one value, and the dangerous one is 'this job is malformed' -- a census reading invalid=4 teaches the next reader to skim past it (the alarm-fatigue class this repo grades P1)."}
